1
00:00:01,453 --> 00:00:04,192
(Who's Going to Win?)

2
00:00:04,193 --> 00:00:07,562
- Nice to see you. - Nice to see you.

3
00:00:07,563 --> 00:00:08,762
By the way, you got injured...

4
00:00:08,763 --> 00:00:10,032
- while running. - Yes.

5
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:12,832
- That happened last week. - You were quite fast.

6
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:13,833
Ready...

7
00:00:14,103 --> 00:00:17,743
(Hyun Moo and Sung Hwan had a race in the middle of the night.)

8
00:00:19,143 --> 00:00:21,573
(Moosain Bolt won the race.)

9
00:00:22,413 --> 00:00:24,273
(And after a cutthroat match, )

10
00:00:25,013 --> 00:00:27,483
(the two runners ended up with injuries.)

11
00:00:27,853 --> 00:00:29,153
It bled a lot that day.

12
00:00:30,053 --> 00:00:31,252
How could you get an injury...

13
00:00:31,253 --> 00:00:32,482
- only after a short race? - Well,

14
00:00:32,483 --> 00:00:34,253
- it shows you did your best. - Right.

15
00:00:34,393 --> 00:00:35,952
- You didn't go easy on him. - As if his life depended on it.

16
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:38,162
I hope this will give us a chance to hold a sports day.

17
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:39,423
With these jokers?

18
00:00:39,663 --> 00:00:41,162
Hyun Moo is a fast runner.

19
00:00:41,163 --> 00:00:43,163
Let's do it once the weather gets better in fall.

20
00:00:43,463 --> 00:00:45,202
I need to dominate CODE KUNST with my soccer skills too.

21
00:00:45,203 --> 00:00:46,203
- Right. - CODE KUNST?

22
00:00:46,663 --> 00:00:48,132
- I'll show you how I get past him. - I can beat you...

23
00:00:48,133 --> 00:00:49,502
even in high heels.

24
00:00:49,503 --> 00:00:51,403
- High heels? - I'll wear higher heels than you.

25
00:00:52,043 --> 00:00:53,502
(Sure. We couldn't care less who wins.)

26
00:00:53,503 --> 00:00:54,543
My gosh.

27
00:00:54,973 --> 00:00:57,373
(Break Ground with the First Shovel at Last)

28
00:00:58,343 --> 00:01:01,582
(Hyun Moo is sleeping soundly.)

29
00:01:01,583 --> 00:01:03,183
(Squirming)

30
00:01:05,423 --> 00:01:08,423
(Turning)

31
00:01:09,623 --> 00:01:12,963
(He lets out a big yawn.)

32
00:01:14,493 --> 00:01:17,163
(He gets up.)

33
00:01:17,463 --> 00:01:19,162
Is it because you have a lot of machines at home?

34
00:01:19,163 --> 00:01:20,803
It looks like a VIP room at a hospital.

35
00:01:22,003 --> 00:01:23,372
- Doesn't it? - What are you wearing?

36
00:01:23,373 --> 00:01:25,272
- His pajamas look like pillows. - His clothes too.

37
00:01:25,273 --> 00:01:26,672
- What kind of pajamas are they? - Is that...

38
00:01:26,673 --> 00:01:27,872
- part of the blanket? - A VIP patient.

39
00:01:27,873 --> 00:01:29,613
It looks like it's a set with a diaper.

40
00:01:30,773 --> 00:01:33,012
It looks like you're only wearing a diaper like the Boss Baby.

41
00:01:33,013 --> 00:01:34,043
- I look so cute. - Right.

42
00:01:35,083 --> 00:01:36,653
(Laughing)

43
00:01:37,483 --> 00:01:40,023
(Baby Moomoo wakes up with fatigue.)

44
00:01:42,623 --> 00:01:43,623
(Humming)

45
00:01:44,963 --> 00:01:46,022
- What? - What's that?

46
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:47,023
Seriously?

47
00:01:47,024 --> 00:01:48,892
There's always something new in his house.

48
00:01:48,893 --> 00:01:50,832
(A strange object is placed in a corner of his bedroom.)

49
00:01:50,833 --> 00:01:52,632
- What's that? - It happens every time. Seriously.

50
00:01:52,633 --> 00:01:54,132
Is that a studio set or something?

51
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:57,332
(Is that not a real house?)

52
00:01:57,333 --> 00:01:58,772
- Do you live in a cafe? - How could you say that?

53
00:01:58,773 --> 00:02:00,042
There's always something new in your house.

54
00:02:00,043 --> 00:02:02,312
It's been a while since my house was on TV.

55
00:02:02,313 --> 00:02:03,342
Seriously. This is too much.

56
00:02:03,343 --> 00:02:04,343
- It's driving me crazy. - Yes.

57
00:02:04,344 --> 00:02:05,712
You see this in corporate buildings.

58
00:02:05,713 --> 00:02:06,912
- Right. - In their lobbies and stuff.

59
00:02:06,913 --> 00:02:07,982
Yes, you see in lobbies.

60
00:02:07,983 --> 00:02:09,052
- And it spurts out water. - You know what?

61
00:02:09,053 --> 00:02:10,512
You see that kind of wall at dermatology clinics too.

62
00:02:10,513 --> 00:02:12,322
- Right. - Hospitals and subway stations too.

63
00:02:12,323 --> 00:02:13,852
- Or at cafes. - Yes.

64
00:02:13,853 --> 00:02:14,952
You also see it in a subway station.

65
00:02:14,953 --> 00:02:16,422
Then do you live in a subway station?

66
00:02:16,423 --> 00:02:17,692
I don't live in a subway station.

67
00:02:17,693 --> 00:02:18,693
- What... - But...

68
00:02:18,694 --> 00:02:20,162
I dreamed of doing this.

69
00:02:20,163 --> 00:02:21,932
Designing an entire wall of my bedroom with plants.

70
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:23,892
I knew you and I would see eye to eye on this, Dae Ja Yeon.

71
00:02:23,893 --> 00:02:26,133
(She's indeed Dae Ja Yeon.)

72
00:02:27,203 --> 00:02:29,802
I'm crazy about greens and plants.

73
00:02:29,803 --> 00:02:31,403
I did all sorts of things to my house.

74
00:02:31,543 --> 00:02:34,303
I tried to grow plants, but I ended up killing them all.

75
00:02:35,043 --> 00:02:36,842
I tried everything a long time ago.

76
00:02:36,843 --> 00:02:39,312
I had plants that supposedly never died, but I killed them.

77
00:02:39,313 --> 00:02:41,283
- You don't mix well with plants. - How beautiful.

78
00:02:41,813 --> 00:02:43,412
- My plants in a three-tier cart... - I remember that.

79
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:44,852
- also died. - All of them died too.

80
00:02:44,853 --> 00:02:46,482
People rarely kill those plants.

81
00:02:46,483 --> 00:02:47,553
All of them died.

82
00:02:47,823 --> 00:02:50,823
I thought I would never be able to grow plants.

83
00:02:51,293 --> 00:02:53,623
But there's an agency that takes care of plants on my behalf.

84
00:02:55,293 --> 00:02:56,762
I can just pay a monthly fee.

85
00:02:56,763 --> 00:02:59,633
They regularly come to my house, trim my plants,

86
00:02:59,933 --> 00:03:01,163
and change the water.

87
00:03:01,403 --> 00:03:04,432
My plants are still alive thanks to the agency's help.

88
00:03:04,433 --> 00:03:06,672
- He sounds like a rich Indian man. - He outsources it.

89
00:03:06,673 --> 00:03:08,912
Of course, I have a desire to grow plants.

90
00:03:08,913 --> 00:03:10,812
But my throat is never in good condition.

91
00:03:10,813 --> 00:03:12,213
So keeping it hydrated is very important.

92
00:03:12,683 --> 00:03:14,082
I hear a natural humidifier...

93
00:03:14,083 --> 00:03:16,113
is more helpful than a machine.

94
00:03:16,413 --> 00:03:17,882
I'm growing NASA-approved plants...

95
00:03:17,883 --> 00:03:19,583
- that are known to purify air. - Come on.

96
00:03:21,083 --> 00:03:23,893
(He breathes in nature as soon as he wakes up.)

97
00:03:24,793 --> 00:03:26,763
- Anyway, the leaves are beautiful. - Right.

98
00:03:26,923 --> 00:03:28,162
- It's a type of philodendron. - I hear...

99
00:03:28,163 --> 00:03:29,462
- there are snakes too. - Right, that's the one.

100
00:03:29,463 --> 00:03:31,133
- Phil-something. - Right.

101
00:03:32,463 --> 00:03:33,832
That's beautiful, isn't it?

102
00:03:33,833 --> 00:03:35,273
(He feels the leaves with love although he doesn't know its name.)

103
00:03:37,033 --> 00:03:38,502
(He breathes in deeply through his nose.)

104
00:03:38,503 --> 00:03:40,572
But they don't have a special scent.

105
00:03:40,573 --> 00:03:42,543
Right. I bet it doesn't smell like anything.

106
00:03:43,713 --> 00:03:44,913
- He's blowing his nose. - Yes.

107
00:03:46,083 --> 00:03:47,612
(I'm not blowing my nose. I just love my plants.)

108
00:03:47,613 --> 00:03:48,853
I'm crazy about plants.

109
00:03:49,753 --> 00:03:51,683
(I love plants so much.)

110
00:03:51,853 --> 00:03:54,053
They're going strong.

111
00:03:55,293 --> 00:03:56,393
(Humming)

112
00:03:57,423 --> 00:03:58,463
That...

113
00:03:59,463 --> 00:04:00,523
- There's another one? - My gosh.

114
00:04:02,393 --> 00:04:05,233
(I have one in my living room too.)

115
00:04:05,833 --> 00:04:06,862
- Wait. - Why...

116
00:04:06,863 --> 00:04:08,502
Did the plants go through the floor...

117
00:04:08,503 --> 00:04:09,803
and spread on the wall in the living room?

118
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:10,933
What?

119
00:04:10,934 --> 00:04:13,043
You don't know how much I adore them. What?

120
00:04:13,203 --> 00:04:15,812
- It's funny because it's too much. - This is too much.

121
00:04:15,813 --> 00:04:17,042
- Why is this too much? - Are there more plants...

122
00:04:17,043 --> 00:04:18,383
- inside your fridge? - No.

123
00:04:18,483 --> 00:04:20,482
Let me be honest now. You know what this looks like to me?

124
00:04:20,483 --> 00:04:22,683
You look like a guy who's living in the bunker after the apocalypse.

125
00:04:23,413 --> 00:04:25,282
Seriously. It does look like a scene from "2001: A Space Odyssey."

126
00:04:25,283 --> 00:04:26,482
(It was released in 1968.)

127
00:04:26,483 --> 00:04:28,752
- Seriously. - Mankind after 1,000 years...

128
00:04:28,753 --> 00:04:30,693
- It's like an old sci-fi movie. - Like this.

129
00:04:31,323 --> 00:04:33,793
- I bet he's like 300 years old. - Right.

130
00:04:35,463 --> 00:04:36,832
Gosh, why is this so funny?

131
00:04:36,833 --> 00:04:39,633
(He can't stop touching them as he deeply cares for them.)

132
00:04:39,833 --> 00:04:41,472
Do you know how to prune them?

133
00:04:41,473 --> 00:04:43,372
- Some of them dried up. - I see.

134
00:04:43,373 --> 00:04:44,502
They need to go.

135
00:04:44,503 --> 00:04:46,502
Is it funny because of his pajamas? Why is this so funny?

136
00:04:46,503 --> 00:04:48,343
Doesn't he look like he's part of a new mankind?

137
00:04:48,843 --> 00:04:51,642
- He looks like a different species. - Yes.

138
00:04:51,643 --> 00:04:52,643
Right.

139
00:04:54,883 --> 00:04:58,553
(Moomoo of the different species continues to stay busy.)

140
00:04:59,183 --> 00:05:02,593
(He gets the juicer ready.)

141
00:05:03,053 --> 00:05:04,223
(Opening)

142
00:05:08,463 --> 00:05:09,792
That looks good.

143
00:05:09,793 --> 00:05:11,662
- The bag comes with celery... - Celery.

144
00:05:11,663 --> 00:05:13,232
- and apples. - I see.

145
00:05:13,233 --> 00:05:14,333
They're very healthy.

146
00:05:15,103 --> 00:05:17,103
(He washes the vegetables from the bag...)

147
00:05:17,573 --> 00:05:19,043
(and adds them to the juicer.)

148
00:05:19,803 --> 00:05:21,442
I can't believe this is my breakfast.

149
00:05:21,443 --> 00:05:22,713
(He starts his breakfast with vegetables and fruits.)

150
00:05:23,043 --> 00:05:24,743
Your diet has gotten so healthy.

151
00:05:25,783 --> 00:05:27,213
(Pressing down)

152
00:05:28,553 --> 00:05:30,683
(It starts operating.)

153
00:05:31,953 --> 00:05:33,023
Extract.

154
00:05:33,683 --> 00:05:35,052
- When it starts extracting... - That's fascinating.

155
00:05:35,053 --> 00:05:36,053
Watch.

156
00:05:36,054 --> 00:05:37,252
(It gives me tasty juice.)

157
00:05:37,253 --> 00:05:38,792
- It's extracting the juice, right? - It is.

158
00:05:38,793 --> 00:05:41,493
You don't have to remove the seeds. It only gives you the extract.

159
00:05:42,163 --> 00:05:44,433
I only get the extract, and the solids come out separately.

160
00:05:44,963 --> 00:05:46,303
I must drink up the last drop too.

161
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:47,933
Come on out.

162
00:05:48,903 --> 00:05:50,173
This is so convenient.

163
00:05:51,273 --> 00:05:53,343
(He has a sip of the juice that has greens he likes.)

164
00:05:53,473 --> 00:05:54,473
(Hitting the spot)

165
00:05:54,603 --> 00:05:56,712
I can drink the extract of vegetables and fruits together.

166
00:05:56,713 --> 00:05:58,882
The latest trend is enzyme juice.

167
00:05:58,883 --> 00:05:59,883
Really? What's that?

168
00:05:59,884 --> 00:06:01,082
- It's enzyme-rich juice. - Enzyme?

169
00:06:01,083 --> 00:06:02,513
I'm leading that trend now.

170
00:06:04,753 --> 00:06:05,952
That hits the spot. My gosh.

171
00:06:05,953 --> 00:06:07,553
(That was great juice.)

172
00:06:08,523 --> 00:06:09,693
I should get changed now.

173
00:06:11,663 --> 00:06:12,892
I'm going to be busy today.

174
00:06:12,893 --> 00:06:13,993
(Hyun Moo comes out after getting changed.)

175
00:06:15,263 --> 00:06:16,893
- The previous outfit was funny. - Right.

176
00:06:17,263 --> 00:06:19,332
- He should've worn it outside. - You should've kept it on.

177
00:06:19,333 --> 00:06:20,762
(Disappointed)

178
00:06:20,763 --> 00:06:22,732
People will report me, thinking I'm a lunatic.

179
00:06:22,733 --> 00:06:23,933
(People will report me.)

180
00:06:26,403 --> 00:06:27,472
(He sets out in an outfit he won't get reported in.)

181
00:06:27,473 --> 00:06:28,513
It's raining.

182
00:06:29,613 --> 00:06:32,083
(The road is wet from the rain.)

183
00:06:34,283 --> 00:06:36,012
(Don't you try me, I want some more)

184
00:06:36,013 --> 00:06:37,182
Are you reciting the Buddhist chant?

185
00:06:37,183 --> 00:06:39,223
(The Buddhist rapping resonates through the humidity.)

186
00:06:40,953 --> 00:06:43,052
(He heads somewhere while humming endlessly.)

187
00:06:43,053 --> 00:06:44,553
I can never copy her rap.

188
00:06:46,893 --> 00:06:48,393
- Gimpo? - The airport?

189
00:06:53,363 --> 00:06:55,173
- Hey, Hyun Moo. - Can you talk now?

190
00:06:55,303 --> 00:06:56,973
Sure. I can talk. Go ahead.

191
00:06:57,303 --> 00:06:59,143
I'm heading to Gimpo now.

192
00:06:59,273 --> 00:07:01,373
- Really? - Are you in Gimpo now?

193
00:07:01,713 --> 00:07:02,943
Yes, I am.

194
00:07:03,413 --> 00:07:04,472
(By 100 of KOYOTE, a resident of Gimpo)

195
00:07:04,473 --> 00:07:05,543
- My gosh. - It's By 100.

196
00:07:07,113 --> 00:07:10,353
(The main rapper of KOYOTE, an influential group of his day)

197
00:07:11,113 --> 00:07:13,352
(And he enjoys a healthy lifestyle in his neighborhood.)

198
00:07:13,353 --> 00:07:14,353
- Right? - Yes.

199
00:07:14,653 --> 00:07:16,392
I didn't know he lived in Gimpo.

200
00:07:16,393 --> 00:07:17,453
He's been living there for a long time.

201
00:07:17,953 --> 00:07:20,623
Remember what I told you the other day?

202
00:07:20,963 --> 00:07:23,162
That I was looking into a house in Gimpo.

203
00:07:23,163 --> 00:07:24,432
- What? - Yes.

204
00:07:24,433 --> 00:07:25,732
Are you going to move?

205
00:07:25,733 --> 00:07:28,003
I'm thinking about moving. I'm entertaining the idea.

206
00:07:28,233 --> 00:07:30,072
I've been looking into some houses for 2 to 3 months.

207
00:07:30,073 --> 00:07:31,102
- A house there? - Yes.

208
00:07:31,103 --> 00:07:34,073
But don't you have more things to do around Gangnam?

209
00:07:34,273 --> 00:07:36,843
When I thought about it, I rarely did things in Gangnam.

210
00:07:37,213 --> 00:07:38,843
I have to come to Sangam or Yeouido for work.

211
00:07:39,183 --> 00:07:41,212
You come to Sangam often. So Gimpo makes sense.

212
00:07:41,213 --> 00:07:42,213
- Yes. - Right.

213
00:07:42,214 --> 00:07:44,713
Here's the kind of house I want.

214
00:07:45,153 --> 00:07:47,152
- Okay. - A house with...

215
00:07:47,153 --> 00:07:49,953
my own private garden.

216
00:07:50,453 --> 00:07:52,862
A house with a small yard. You know what I mean?

217
00:07:52,863 --> 00:07:54,393
It doesn't need to be big.

218
00:07:54,863 --> 00:07:56,863
I've been interested in a house in the suburbs for a while now.

219
00:07:56,993 --> 00:07:58,262
In the entertainment industry,

220
00:07:58,263 --> 00:08:00,363
I meet a lot of celebrities who live in a suburban home.

221
00:08:00,633 --> 00:08:01,972
I'm so envious of them...

222
00:08:01,973 --> 00:08:03,303
because I lived my entire life in apartments.

223
00:08:03,633 --> 00:08:06,573
I want to grow my own vegetables like Na Rae.

224
00:08:06,773 --> 00:08:07,842
I really want to try it.

225
00:08:07,843 --> 00:08:08,942
A vegetable garden?

226
00:08:08,943 --> 00:08:10,273
You're busy, but you manage.

227
00:08:10,673 --> 00:08:14,182
Even Kian84 has some outdoor space on the rooftop.

228
00:08:14,183 --> 00:08:15,713
(Kian84 also has a rooftop.)

229
00:08:17,153 --> 00:08:18,423
- Why did they use that clip? - The rooftop.

230
00:08:18,683 --> 00:08:20,853
I want a place where I can end my day...

231
00:08:21,183 --> 00:08:22,822
while watching the sunset...

232
00:08:22,823 --> 00:08:24,553
and enjoying the soft breeze.

233
00:08:24,893 --> 00:08:26,493
When I stayed in the hanok a few years ago,

234
00:08:26,593 --> 00:08:28,732
I woke up to the chirping of the birds.

235
00:08:28,733 --> 00:08:30,992
- I still remember that. - Right. You loved that experience.

236
00:08:30,993 --> 00:08:32,062
Gosh, who is that?

237
00:08:32,063 --> 00:08:33,362
(His memory in the outdoor space is unforgettable.)

238
00:08:33,363 --> 00:08:34,873
I think I like looking at greens.

239
00:08:35,503 --> 00:08:37,302
(He enjoys looking at greens, )

240
00:08:37,303 --> 00:08:39,072
(eating the greens, )

241
00:08:39,073 --> 00:08:41,503
(and growing the greens.)

242
00:08:42,043 --> 00:08:43,612
I prefer mountains to the sea.

243
00:08:43,613 --> 00:08:44,743
(I prefer mountains to the sea.)

244
00:08:44,943 --> 00:08:47,213
When I look at greenery, it truly relaxes me.

245
00:08:47,583 --> 00:08:50,313
I want to live close to nature.

246
00:08:51,083 --> 00:08:52,523
You know what? My mother...

247
00:08:53,053 --> 00:08:55,353
- Yes. - lives in Gangseo-gu.

248
00:08:55,553 --> 00:08:57,493
- My house is in Samseong-dong. - Yes.

249
00:08:57,923 --> 00:08:59,092
We live so far from each other.

250
00:08:59,093 --> 00:09:00,263
- Right. - It is far.

251
00:09:00,323 --> 00:09:01,763
Gimpo is closer to my mom's place.

252
00:09:01,963 --> 00:09:02,963
Is that so?

253
00:09:03,133 --> 00:09:05,063
My mother keeps coming to my house.

254
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:07,062
For the sake of my mother's safety,

255
00:09:07,063 --> 00:09:08,633
I thought I should move closer to her.

256
00:09:08,803 --> 00:09:12,343
It was 2 years ago. I declared it in 2023.

257
00:09:12,673 --> 00:09:15,073
It's my five-year plan to be a good son to my mom.

258
00:09:16,213 --> 00:09:20,183
I'm thinking of breaking ground on my project in Gimpo.

259
00:09:21,243 --> 00:09:22,782
The first thing he does is moving.

260
00:09:22,783 --> 00:09:23,952
(Looking determined)

261
00:09:23,953 --> 00:09:25,022
I'm sure you can find simpler tasks...

262
00:09:25,023 --> 00:09:26,082
- to make her happy. - Right.

263
00:09:26,083 --> 00:09:28,752
Taking pictures with your mom should be enough as the first task.

264
00:09:28,753 --> 00:09:30,222
That won't satisfy me.

265
00:09:30,223 --> 00:09:31,792
- What? - It's nothing special.

266
00:09:31,793 --> 00:09:33,193
You want to pull out all the stops?

267
00:09:33,863 --> 00:09:34,933
Yes.

268
00:09:36,963 --> 00:09:40,463
(After winning the Grand Award at the MBC Entertainment Awards, )

269
00:09:41,303 --> 00:09:43,633
(Moomoo became the variety show princess.)

270
00:09:44,173 --> 00:09:45,702
(And he made a new resolution for his next goal.)

271
00:09:45,703 --> 00:09:47,143
(Fulfilling his duty as a son)

272
00:09:47,743 --> 00:09:49,743
(He gave himself 5 years to complete the project.)

273
00:09:49,943 --> 00:09:51,113
My five years aren't up.

274
00:09:51,213 --> 00:09:54,182
(Afterward, time moved quickly.)

275
00:09:54,183 --> 00:09:56,053
You made that promise a long time ago.

276
00:09:56,383 --> 00:09:57,883
(And 2025 has come.)

277
00:09:58,483 --> 00:10:00,083
(My mother comes to my house.)

278
00:10:00,853 --> 00:10:03,352
(I pile up all the dirty dishes then.)

279
00:10:03,353 --> 00:10:04,653
(Appalled)

280
00:10:05,963 --> 00:10:08,732
(His will to be a good son continued to burn brightly.)

281
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:09,793
The icon of a bad son.

282
00:10:10,633 --> 00:10:14,233
(He watched how other members fulfilled their duty as children.)

283
00:10:14,903 --> 00:10:16,032
When I watched these clips,

284
00:10:16,033 --> 00:10:18,773
- I learned a lot. - Of course. My gosh.

285
00:10:19,043 --> 00:10:22,572
She comes to my house once every two weeks.

286
00:10:22,573 --> 00:10:24,072
She comes so often.

287
00:10:24,073 --> 00:10:26,183
My house is already clean, but she comes to clean anyway.

288
00:10:26,513 --> 00:10:28,113
"I doubt you did a proper job of cleaning."

289
00:10:28,313 --> 00:10:29,482
(Cleaning)

290
00:10:29,483 --> 00:10:30,983
She doesn't believe in the robot vacuum cleaner.

291
00:10:31,253 --> 00:10:34,283
There's no point. She'll come and clean my house herself anyway.

292
00:10:34,453 --> 00:10:36,153
There's no point in washing the dishes.

293
00:10:36,493 --> 00:10:38,052
She takes out all the plates and washes them again.

294
00:10:38,053 --> 00:10:40,423
That's why I decided to pile them up.

295
00:10:41,523 --> 00:10:42,863
"Okay. Go ahead."

296
00:10:43,433 --> 00:10:45,903
Seriously. She really does that. It drives me crazy.

297
00:10:46,033 --> 00:10:47,962
I called two of my friends...

298
00:10:47,963 --> 00:10:49,733
and deep-cleaned my house. It was spotless.

299
00:10:50,033 --> 00:10:51,302
There wasn't a speck of dust.

300
00:10:51,303 --> 00:10:53,402
But she still came and complained the house was dirty.

301
00:10:53,403 --> 00:10:54,503
And she cleaned all over again.

302
00:10:54,803 --> 00:10:56,312
Moms have a different cleaning standard...

303
00:10:56,313 --> 00:10:58,343
- than we do. - It's a bit different.

304
00:10:58,543 --> 00:10:59,913
- Right. - It's totally different.

305
00:11:00,243 --> 00:11:03,252
I think she does that, so she can be part of your life.

306
00:11:03,253 --> 00:11:04,613
- That's true. - Right.

307
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:08,222
I thought this would be too much work on my mom.

308
00:11:08,223 --> 00:11:09,622
But I think it's some kind of itch.

309
00:11:09,623 --> 00:11:11,763
It's impossible to talk to her about this.

310
00:11:12,123 --> 00:11:15,363
Living close to her is the best way to fulfill my duty as her son.

311
00:11:16,163 --> 00:11:17,993
- Hey. Then... - Yes.

312
00:11:18,233 --> 00:11:20,402
Do you have any advice for me?

313
00:11:20,403 --> 00:11:22,472
Or do you want to come and check out my house briefly?

314
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:24,072
Okay. I'm on my way then.

315
00:11:24,073 --> 00:11:25,073
(Okay, I'm in.)

316
00:11:25,074 --> 00:11:26,442
- Now? - Yes.

317
00:11:26,443 --> 00:11:28,573
- Text me the address. - Sure.

318
00:11:30,173 --> 00:11:31,712
Gosh, Gimpo is nice.

319
00:11:31,713 --> 00:11:32,713
(I have a good feeling about this.)

320
00:11:33,783 --> 00:11:35,513
(He then makes another call.)

321
00:11:35,613 --> 00:11:36,753
Sook.

322
00:11:37,113 --> 00:11:39,023
Hyun Moo. Where are you now?

323
00:11:39,283 --> 00:11:41,423
- I... - A lot of celebrities live there.

324
00:11:41,523 --> 00:11:43,353
- She used to live there, but not now. - Right.

325
00:11:43,593 --> 00:11:45,823
I'm going to Gimpo to look at houses. I told you.

326
00:11:45,993 --> 00:11:48,362
Oh, yes. Right. You did.

327
00:11:48,363 --> 00:11:50,133
- I was on the phone with By 100. - Yes.

328
00:11:50,863 --> 00:11:53,462
- Yes. You must ask us about Gimpo. - He...

329
00:11:53,463 --> 00:11:56,773
Right. That's why I called you before I checked out some houses.

330
00:11:56,903 --> 00:11:59,173
You can buy a house toward Mount Modam.

331
00:11:59,373 --> 00:12:00,602
Mount Modam?

332
00:12:00,603 --> 00:12:02,372
But what kind of house do you want?

333
00:12:02,373 --> 00:12:04,412
I've lived in all kinds of houses.

334
00:12:04,413 --> 00:12:05,682
I first moved into an apartment...

335
00:12:05,683 --> 00:12:06,943
- in Gimpo. - Okay.

336
00:12:07,183 --> 00:12:08,683
- Then I lived in a rooftop house. - Okay.

337
00:12:08,853 --> 00:12:10,482
Lastly, I lived in a house with a yard.

338
00:12:10,483 --> 00:12:11,552
Right.

339
00:12:11,553 --> 00:12:14,853
People say they move to Gimpo first before moving to the countryside.

340
00:12:15,053 --> 00:12:16,692
You lived on the rooftop, but it wasn't satisfying.

341
00:12:16,693 --> 00:12:18,193
- You moved to a house with a yard. - Right.

342
00:12:18,523 --> 00:12:20,822
You have to check out the houses and then make a decision.

343
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:22,132
- Okay. - Yes.

344
00:12:22,133 --> 00:12:23,232
Good luck with house hunting.

345
00:12:23,233 --> 00:12:25,503
- Okay. Thank you. Okay. - Call me if you have questions.

346
00:12:26,233 --> 00:12:27,603
Gosh, why is it raining?

347
00:12:28,533 --> 00:12:31,003
It's pouring down. Come on.

348
00:12:32,543 --> 00:12:35,473
(He starts to see some houses now.)

349
00:12:36,643 --> 00:12:38,542
(Pop-eyed)

350
00:12:38,543 --> 00:12:39,743
This place doesn't look like Korea.

351
00:12:41,143 --> 00:12:42,583
It looks like houses you'd see in "Surprise Mystery TV."

352
00:12:42,953 --> 00:12:44,212
Gosh, nice.

353
00:12:44,213 --> 00:12:45,622
I've never been to a place like that.

354
00:12:45,623 --> 00:12:47,923
My gosh. I had no idea there was a place like this.

355
00:12:49,193 --> 00:12:50,252
This must be the one.

356
00:12:50,253 --> 00:12:51,253
(He arrives at By 100's house.)

357
00:12:52,023 --> 00:12:54,263
(Looking around)

358
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:56,763
This is the one.

359
00:12:57,833 --> 00:12:59,763
I'm just barging into his house.

360
00:13:00,063 --> 00:13:01,502
- I see. - That's By 100's house?

361
00:13:01,503 --> 00:13:03,233
- Yes, it's his house. - It looks like a house from abroad.

362
00:13:03,633 --> 00:13:05,743
This is the kind of house you'd see abroad.

363
00:13:06,743 --> 00:13:07,773
It's better than I thought.

364
00:13:08,673 --> 00:13:10,573
- Hey, Mr. By 100. - Yes.

365
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:14,543
(Chuckling)

366
00:13:14,544 --> 00:13:15,653
You're here.

367
00:13:16,813 --> 00:13:17,853
You're here.

368
00:13:18,013 --> 00:13:20,182
- You were sleeping for real. - Yes.

369
00:13:20,183 --> 00:13:22,393
I was home anyway. So it's no big deal.

370
00:13:23,393 --> 00:13:24,422
Come on in.

371
00:13:24,423 --> 00:13:26,893
My gosh, look at your house. It looks great.

372
00:13:27,693 --> 00:13:30,032
- He decorated his place so nicely. - Look at this.

373
00:13:30,033 --> 00:13:31,692
- He's stylish, to begin with. - He's stylish.

374
00:13:31,693 --> 00:13:32,903
He has a good eye for interior design.

375
00:13:33,803 --> 00:13:35,903
(He fills the house with soft lights from indirect lighting.)

376
00:13:36,703 --> 00:13:38,842
(Boosting the hip vibe with unique props)

377
00:13:38,843 --> 00:13:41,273
Your house has a nice vibe. That's Chet Baker.

378
00:13:42,343 --> 00:13:44,772
- This was a surprise visit. - Yes.

379
00:13:44,773 --> 00:13:46,512
- I'm checking out houses... - Okay.

380
00:13:46,513 --> 00:13:47,943
- in different areas. - Okay.

381
00:13:48,143 --> 00:13:49,712
- You already checked out places. - I called Sook earlier.

382
00:13:49,713 --> 00:13:51,352
- I got a lot of advice from her. - There's also...

383
00:13:51,353 --> 00:13:53,223
a new residential housing complex.

384
00:13:53,483 --> 00:13:54,522
- I don't know. - The one with a yard.

385
00:13:54,523 --> 00:13:55,692
- I don't know. - You don't?

386
00:13:55,693 --> 00:13:57,052
- No. - So that's one of the options.

387
00:13:57,053 --> 00:13:59,623
I also saw a few red-brick houses.

388
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:02,363
My mother's house is close from here.

389
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,493
It will be easier for my mother to visit me.

390
00:14:04,733 --> 00:14:06,932
She likes having a vegetable garden.

391
00:14:06,933 --> 00:14:09,333
But both of us live in apartments.

392
00:14:09,503 --> 00:14:10,732
I'm serious about this.

393
00:14:10,733 --> 00:14:11,972
- I kept telling you about this. - Yes.

394
00:14:11,973 --> 00:14:13,542
- So you're serious? - Yes.

395
00:14:13,543 --> 00:14:14,543
(Come on.)

396
00:14:15,003 --> 00:14:16,442
(The homeowner is still sleepy as he just woke up.)

397
00:14:16,443 --> 00:14:17,972
He lost a lot of his linguistic skills.

398
00:14:17,973 --> 00:14:20,243
- Well... - Can you give me a tour?

399
00:14:20,383 --> 00:14:21,613
- Of my house? - Yes.

400
00:14:21,983 --> 00:14:23,482
- You don't mind, right? - Sure.

401
00:14:23,483 --> 00:14:25,013
This is the living room. That's the kitchen.

402
00:14:26,083 --> 00:14:27,823
He has a beautiful home.

403
00:14:30,093 --> 00:14:32,993
That's the laundry room. Do you call that a pantry?

404
00:14:33,123 --> 00:14:34,422
- Sure. Probably. - I have a room there.

405
00:14:34,423 --> 00:14:38,133
- Then I have a yard. - Where's the yard?

406
00:14:38,233 --> 00:14:39,532
It's in the back here.

407
00:14:39,533 --> 00:14:41,263
There's a yard in the front.

408
00:14:41,403 --> 00:14:42,473
I love yards.

409
00:14:43,033 --> 00:14:45,543
It used to be full of grass. But I cleared it out.

410
00:14:46,824 --> 00:14:49,394
It used to be full of grass. But I cleared it out.

411
00:14:50,494 --> 00:14:51,833
- That's what you want the most. - Yes.

412
00:14:51,834 --> 00:14:54,033
But I put in tiles this year.

413
00:14:54,034 --> 00:14:56,973
Okay. So you have plants here. This is your garden.

414
00:14:56,974 --> 00:14:58,404
Isn't that great? No one can see you.

415
00:14:58,774 --> 00:15:00,874
It must be easy to manage the space.

416
00:15:01,974 --> 00:15:03,673
It used to be full of grass before.

417
00:15:03,674 --> 00:15:04,773
- But I got rid of it. - I see.

418
00:15:04,774 --> 00:15:06,613
- You got rid of it and added tiles? - I did. Right.

419
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:08,313
- Yes. It used to have... - You have barbecue parties here.

420
00:15:08,314 --> 00:15:09,354
Yes.

421
00:15:09,484 --> 00:15:12,023
And I grow my plants here.

422
00:15:12,024 --> 00:15:14,583
- Okay. Darn birds? - Those darn birds...

423
00:15:14,584 --> 00:15:16,724
ate up all of my blueberries, so I covered them up.

424
00:15:17,154 --> 00:15:18,253
But they ate through the net.

425
00:15:18,254 --> 00:15:19,364
- He's... - So I have nothing there.

426
00:15:19,624 --> 00:15:21,594
They ripped the net while I was in Sydney.

427
00:15:21,924 --> 00:15:24,034
- They must find food somehow. - Right.

428
00:15:24,164 --> 00:15:25,933
- This place is great. - Yes.

429
00:15:25,934 --> 00:15:27,303
- Yes. - So that's the yard.

430
00:15:27,304 --> 00:15:29,173
- If you want a nice view, - Yes.

431
00:15:29,174 --> 00:15:31,503
You can draw the curtains open. Come here.

432
00:15:31,504 --> 00:15:32,774
(Come this way.)

433
00:15:33,944 --> 00:15:35,944
The mountain is over there.

434
00:15:36,344 --> 00:15:37,443
Is this Mount Modam?

435
00:15:37,444 --> 00:15:38,544
Yes, it is.

436
00:15:39,744 --> 00:15:41,444
- How nice. - It's a floor-to-ceiling window.

437
00:15:41,884 --> 00:15:43,483
The view looks great when it rains and snows.

438
00:15:43,484 --> 00:15:44,513
- I bet. - Yes.

439
00:15:44,514 --> 00:15:45,824
- This window is like a frame. - Yes.

440
00:15:46,354 --> 00:15:49,794
What I liked the most about his house was the greenery.

441
00:15:50,154 --> 00:15:51,454
Trees were everywhere.

442
00:15:52,024 --> 00:15:55,224
- Greenery relaxes me. - You do need that.

443
00:15:55,594 --> 00:15:57,034
I don't care if those birds eat all of my crops.

444
00:15:57,594 --> 00:15:59,264
I can buy blueberries from supermarkets.

445
00:15:59,334 --> 00:16:01,303
Wouldn't it be happier to watch the birds?

446
00:16:01,304 --> 00:16:03,504
Right. The chirping sounds are great too.

447
00:16:03,804 --> 00:16:05,174
I'd welcome animals with open arms.

448
00:16:06,144 --> 00:16:08,573
But you must be ready to face bugs too.

449
00:16:08,574 --> 00:16:09,744
- Right. - Are you okay with bugs?

450
00:16:10,044 --> 00:16:11,574
I'll call a pest-control service.

451
00:16:12,414 --> 00:16:14,343
- I'll exterminate them. - That won't be enough.

452
00:16:14,344 --> 00:16:15,513
- What do I have to do then? - Never.

453
00:16:15,514 --> 00:16:16,654
- That won't do it. - Here's why.

454
00:16:16,854 --> 00:16:18,083
Those services find the source...

455
00:16:18,084 --> 00:16:19,323
- and get rid of the source. - Yes.

456
00:16:19,324 --> 00:16:20,523
- But the source is... - At places like that,

457
00:16:20,524 --> 00:16:22,123
- they just come in from outside. - Right.

458
00:16:22,124 --> 00:16:23,823
- Like friends coming over. - Can't I just raise a frog?

459
00:16:23,824 --> 00:16:24,854
My gosh.

460
00:16:25,124 --> 00:16:26,223
I even thought about that.

461
00:16:26,224 --> 00:16:27,723
- You'll need 2,000 frogs. - What's that?

462
00:16:27,724 --> 00:16:29,463
- Like Venus flytraps. - Gosh, no.

463
00:16:29,464 --> 00:16:31,033
- They won't help? - Not even close.

464
00:16:31,034 --> 00:16:32,933
You need to trap your house with them then.

465
00:16:32,934 --> 00:16:34,963
Can't I just have some house centipedes?

466
00:16:34,964 --> 00:16:36,673
- So... - They'll form a colony.

467
00:16:36,674 --> 00:16:39,873
No. The house centipedes are the weakest bugs...

468
00:16:39,874 --> 00:16:41,744
- They're the nicest ones. - of all the bugs found at homes.

469
00:16:41,844 --> 00:16:44,114
Other bugs that prey on them will come in.

470
00:16:44,274 --> 00:16:45,883
- Like what? - Other centipedes.

471
00:16:45,884 --> 00:16:47,583
- Centipedes. - Scolopendridae with red horns.

472
00:16:47,584 --> 00:16:48,753
- Right. - My gosh.

473
00:16:48,754 --> 00:16:49,984
(That's so scary.)

474
00:16:50,284 --> 00:16:52,753
- Can I go upstairs? - Sure, you can.

475
00:16:52,754 --> 00:16:53,984
(Happily allowing)

476
00:16:56,594 --> 00:16:58,394
(Amazed)

477
00:17:00,324 --> 00:17:02,193
- So this is how it looks upstairs. - This house is great...

478
00:17:02,194 --> 00:17:04,064
for one person.

479
00:17:04,834 --> 00:17:08,034
(At the end of the staircase from the living room, )

480
00:17:09,204 --> 00:17:10,273
(the 2nd-floor space stretches out long.)

481
00:17:10,274 --> 00:17:11,534
(I see!)

482
00:17:12,244 --> 00:17:13,743
This is the master bedroom.

483
00:17:13,744 --> 00:17:14,904
- This is the master bedroom? - Yes.

484
00:17:16,274 --> 00:17:17,343
So...

485
00:17:17,344 --> 00:17:19,184
(Approving)

486
00:17:20,944 --> 00:17:22,353
- Isn't that great? - It's nice and compact.

487
00:17:22,354 --> 00:17:23,384
Yes.

488
00:17:24,014 --> 00:17:26,484
The ceiling is made of glass here.

489
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:28,284
Yes.

490
00:17:28,484 --> 00:17:30,323
I can look at the mountain while having a cup of coffee here.

491
00:17:30,324 --> 00:17:31,794
- Yes. - Then I can see the sky.

492
00:17:32,994 --> 00:17:34,193
- I love this. - I see.

493
00:17:34,194 --> 00:17:35,494
There's a skylight window.

494
00:17:36,334 --> 00:17:37,594
- This is nice. - Yes.

495
00:17:38,864 --> 00:17:40,033
Nice.

496
00:17:40,034 --> 00:17:41,964
- This is the main room. - Yes.

497
00:17:42,334 --> 00:17:44,304
This place is nice. I'm curious about upstairs.

498
00:17:45,774 --> 00:17:47,473
- Gosh, it suddenly got so hot. - Right.

499
00:17:47,474 --> 00:17:51,273
I use this place as storage. I haven't cleaned it up yet.

500
00:17:51,274 --> 00:17:53,914
- The layout is quite unique. - I see.

501
00:17:54,444 --> 00:17:55,683
So this is the rooftop. Gosh, it's hot.

502
00:17:55,684 --> 00:17:57,214
I didn't manage this part of the house.

503
00:17:57,314 --> 00:17:58,884
This is what happens when you don't manage it.

504
00:17:59,224 --> 00:18:01,253
- This happens to your yard. - I see. This happens then.

505
00:18:01,254 --> 00:18:02,653
- You have to clear it out. Right. - Yes.

506
00:18:02,654 --> 00:18:04,353
- My yard looks like that. - I see.

507
00:18:04,354 --> 00:18:06,824
See? Do you think you can manage this?

508
00:18:07,094 --> 00:18:08,194
I loved it.

509
00:18:09,164 --> 00:18:11,294
I can pick some vegetables in the morning like Ja Yeon.

510
00:18:11,634 --> 00:18:13,303
I can pick them on the spot and make a salad.

511
00:18:13,304 --> 00:18:14,934
That's the perfect house for that kind of lifestyle.

512
