00:34:57,004 --> 00:34:58,173
- Not even for your current place? - No.

1017
00:34:58,174 --> 00:35:00,343
- It's a must for buying a place. - How did you buy a place...

1018
00:35:00,344 --> 00:35:01,404
without visiting it?

1019
00:35:01,704 --> 00:35:05,273
I have a story about my current place.

1020
00:35:05,274 --> 00:35:07,384
That place was my dream house.

1021
00:35:07,784 --> 00:35:09,183
- Some places are like that. - It was like that from the start.

1022
00:35:09,184 --> 00:35:11,153
- It's entirely possible. - When I was an announcer,

1023
00:35:11,154 --> 00:35:12,754
I worked as a reporter for "Entertainment Weekly."

1024
00:35:12,984 --> 00:35:14,053
- Back then... - You visited the house back then.

1025
00:35:14,054 --> 00:35:16,183
Back then, I covered a story on Kwon Sang Woo...

1026
00:35:16,184 --> 00:35:17,893
and Son Tae Young's dating rumors.

1027
00:35:17,894 --> 00:35:19,353
- They're married now. - Yes.

1028
00:35:19,354 --> 00:35:21,424
So I visited the apartment one of them lived in.

1029
00:35:21,794 --> 00:35:22,923
Was it Kwon Sang Woo's place?

1030
00:35:22,924 --> 00:35:24,993
- It was a long time ago. - Seriously.

1031
00:35:24,994 --> 00:35:26,093
It's an old story.

1032
00:35:26,094 --> 00:35:27,434
I'm in front of his house.

1033
00:35:27,834 --> 00:35:29,334
- His face is full of greed. - Yes.

1034
00:35:29,634 --> 00:35:31,473
- He was a baby. - He's full of ambition.

1035
00:35:31,474 --> 00:35:33,743
"Hello, I'm here to cover a story..."

1036
00:35:33,744 --> 00:35:36,613
- "on the popular dating rumor." - It's an old story.

1037
00:35:36,614 --> 00:35:37,974
"I'll go inside."

1038
00:35:38,114 --> 00:35:39,574
Then the security guard went, "You can't enter."

1039
00:35:40,014 --> 00:35:41,083
That was what we filmed.

1040
00:35:41,084 --> 00:35:42,143
That's right. We filmed such scenes back in the day.

1041
00:35:42,144 --> 00:35:43,214
Right?

1042
00:35:43,414 --> 00:35:45,584
"Will I be able to live in such a place one day?"

1043
00:35:45,684 --> 00:35:47,584
- I had that thought all my life. - It became a goal.

1044
00:35:47,724 --> 00:35:50,554
Thus, it was my first time checking out multiple properties.

1045
00:35:51,124 --> 00:35:52,654
- It was so exhausting. - It's so exhausting.

1046
00:35:54,594 --> 00:35:57,064
This isn't easy. I can't make up my mind.

1047
00:35:57,164 --> 00:35:58,234
I'm hungry.

1048
00:36:00,504 --> 00:36:01,533
My goodness.

1049
00:36:01,534 --> 00:36:02,704
(Suppressing his hunger, he arrives at a place.)

1050
00:36:03,234 --> 00:36:04,234
(Groaning)

1051
00:36:04,374 --> 00:36:05,474
I'm exhausted.

1052
00:36:07,544 --> 00:36:09,544
It isn't easy to visit properties.

1053
00:36:10,574 --> 00:36:11,873
Why am I so exhausted?

1054
00:36:11,874 --> 00:36:13,213
(He enters a place in an exhausted state.)

1055
00:36:13,214 --> 00:36:15,244
- Hello. - Hello.

1056
00:36:15,484 --> 00:36:17,154
It smells nice.

1057
00:36:17,984 --> 00:36:19,984
- Sook, lastly, - Okay.

1058
00:36:20,424 --> 00:36:21,453
Recommend me a good restaurant in Gimpo.

1059
00:36:21,454 --> 00:36:22,454
She knows many good restaurants.

1060
00:36:22,455 --> 00:36:23,893
Do you like sujebi?

1061
00:36:23,894 --> 00:36:25,853
Eat there. It's so tasty. They sell sujebi.

1062
00:36:25,854 --> 00:36:28,064
- That sounds nice. - Sook is like a machine.

1063
00:36:28,624 --> 00:36:29,863
If I actually move here,

1064
00:36:29,864 --> 00:36:31,063
good restaurants will be important.

1065
00:36:31,064 --> 00:36:33,094
It'll be important to live near the good restaurants.

1066
00:36:33,434 --> 00:36:36,334
So I asked a Gimpo resident, Kim Sook.

1067
00:36:36,974 --> 00:36:38,274
It's a big achievement.

1068
00:36:39,204 --> 00:36:40,604
This is nice.

1069
00:36:41,104 --> 00:36:43,144
Kim Sook recommended the place to me.

1070
00:36:43,544 --> 00:36:45,344
- Thank you. - She said it was a good restaurant.

1071
00:36:45,674 --> 00:36:46,913
I wanted to eat sujebi,

1072
00:36:46,914 --> 00:36:49,213
- but it starts from 2 servings. - Yes. It starts from 2 servings.

1073
00:36:49,214 --> 00:36:51,214
- Okay. I'll order two servings. - There you go.

1074
00:36:51,354 --> 00:36:52,783
What else should I eat?

1075
00:36:52,784 --> 00:36:55,683
This restaurant is famous for grilled half-dried pollack...

1076
00:36:55,684 --> 00:36:56,823
and barley rice.

1077
00:36:56,824 --> 00:36:58,154
Good. I'll get them.

1078
00:36:58,894 --> 00:37:00,663
- I'll cook them well. - Okay.

1079
00:37:00,664 --> 00:37:01,664
Thank you.

1080
00:37:06,971 --> 00:37:08,471
(He enters a restaurant after visiting several properties.)

1081
00:37:12,001 --> 00:37:13,670
(A huge pot of sujebi appears.)

1082
00:37:13,671 --> 00:37:14,741
What's that?

1083
00:37:15,311 --> 00:37:17,281
- It looks so tasty. - This is insane.

1084
00:37:17,711 --> 00:37:20,311
(His eyes go wide.)

1085
00:37:21,351 --> 00:37:24,121
(Grilled half-fried pollack is served next.)

1086
00:37:25,351 --> 00:37:28,221
- Grilled half-fried pollack. - I'm busy looking at the dishes.

1087
00:37:29,521 --> 00:37:30,521
(There is barley rice as well as seasoned vegetables.)

1088
00:37:30,522 --> 00:37:31,561
This is exciting.

1089
00:37:33,491 --> 00:37:35,761
(It's a hearty meal of Korean dishes.)

1090
00:37:36,731 --> 00:37:38,961
I like this place the most.

1091
00:37:39,671 --> 00:37:40,901
You should pick this place.

1092
00:37:41,901 --> 00:37:43,340
The living room is spacious.

1093
00:37:43,341 --> 00:37:44,570
The kitchen is spacious too.

1094
00:37:44,571 --> 00:37:46,241
- It's perfect for partying. - You're right.

1095
00:37:46,571 --> 00:37:48,140
I'll be able to invite about 250 people.

1096
00:37:48,141 --> 00:37:49,410
There are aunties too.

1097
00:37:49,411 --> 00:37:51,341
You could put the chairs together and sleep on them.

1098
00:37:52,141 --> 00:37:53,351
It'll be like a stone bed.

1099
00:37:53,981 --> 00:37:55,051
It'll be nice.

1100
00:37:55,581 --> 00:37:58,121
(The party enthusiast begins eating at the property he visited.)

1101
00:37:59,551 --> 00:38:01,490
(He starts eating the grilled half-dried pollack.)

1102
00:38:01,491 --> 00:38:02,820
- He's making a perilla leaf wrap... - Half-dried pollack.

1103
00:38:02,821 --> 00:38:04,121
- with the half-dried pollack. - It looks moist.

1104
00:38:05,361 --> 00:38:06,490
(Eating)

1105
00:38:06,491 --> 00:38:09,401
The half-dried pollack was both moist and tender.

1106
00:38:12,361 --> 00:38:14,031
The half-dried pollack dish is so tasty.

1107
00:38:16,041 --> 00:38:18,241
Gosh, look at the shrimp.

1108
00:38:20,241 --> 00:38:21,910
- It contains freshwater shrimp. - That's right.

1109
00:38:21,911 --> 00:38:23,681
- That's right. - My goodness.

1110
00:38:23,841 --> 00:38:25,040
- It contains doenjang. - Yes.

1111
00:38:25,041 --> 00:38:26,510
- It's homemade doenjang. - That's right.

1112
00:38:26,511 --> 00:38:28,110
- It looks really delicious. - It's bound to be tasty.

1113
00:38:28,111 --> 00:38:29,851
(He tries the soup reverently.)

1114
00:38:30,181 --> 00:38:31,281
(My goodness)

1115
00:38:33,321 --> 00:38:34,451
It's so tasty.

1116
00:38:34,551 --> 00:38:36,521
Gosh, the shrimp...

1117
00:38:38,091 --> 00:38:40,130
(Eating hurriedly)

1118
00:38:40,131 --> 00:38:41,461
Just pick this place.

1119
00:38:41,631 --> 00:38:43,901
- It's one of the candidates. - This is the best place.

1120
00:38:44,601 --> 00:38:45,931
The shrimp provides the kick.

1121
00:38:47,901 --> 00:38:50,671
(He immediately makes the barley rice bibimbap.)

1122
00:38:51,071 --> 00:38:52,741
Forget about finding a house.

1123
00:38:55,771 --> 00:38:57,210
(He pours in all the seasoned vegetables.)

1124
00:38:57,211 --> 00:38:59,181
- Pour in everything. - That's it.

1125
00:38:59,581 --> 00:39:00,681
Seasoned vegetables don't make you gain weight.

1126
00:39:02,751 --> 00:39:04,050
It looks delicious.

1127
00:39:04,051 --> 00:39:05,081
(Glossy)

1128
00:39:06,251 --> 00:39:08,991
(He takes a big spoonful.)

1129
00:39:10,191 --> 00:39:12,831
(He inhales the food quickly.)

1130
00:39:13,061 --> 00:39:14,131
Barley rice.

1131
00:39:16,501 --> 00:39:18,461
Drink the sujebi soup when food blocks your throat.

1132
00:39:19,501 --> 00:39:20,571
That's it.

1133
00:39:20,931 --> 00:39:22,471
- You speak as if you've watched me. - Yes.

1134
00:39:24,041 --> 00:39:26,011
(Drinking)

1135
00:39:27,111 --> 00:39:28,241
It's so refreshing.

1136
00:39:30,611 --> 00:39:32,911
(He forgets about the stressful task of checking out the properties.)

1137
00:39:33,781 --> 00:39:37,181
(He shoves food down his throat.)

1138
00:39:37,481 --> 00:39:39,691
- My eyes began to go crazy then. - I can see that.

1139
00:39:41,621 --> 00:39:42,960
It's so tasty.

1140
00:39:42,961 --> 00:39:44,321
Sook, thank you.

1141
00:39:46,831 --> 00:39:48,061
He's eating with gusto.

1142
00:39:49,731 --> 00:39:53,131
(He shoves in the taste of Gimpo without a thought.)

1143
00:39:56,141 --> 00:39:57,440
I feel better now.

1144
00:39:57,441 --> 00:39:58,571
I was starving earlier.

1145
00:39:59,811 --> 00:40:00,871
Ma'am.

1146
00:40:02,441 --> 00:40:03,911
Would you please pack this to go?

1147
00:40:03,981 --> 00:40:05,241
- Shall I do that? - Yes.

1148
00:40:05,441 --> 00:40:07,050
- I'll pack it to go. - Thank you.

1149
00:40:07,051 --> 00:40:08,950
(He packs the leftover sujebi to go.)

1150
00:40:08,951 --> 00:40:11,081
(Sweating)

1151
00:40:11,521 --> 00:40:13,050
(He inhaled 4 servings of food.)

1152
00:40:13,051 --> 00:40:14,691
- He enjoyed the food. - He really enjoyed it.

1153
00:40:15,091 --> 00:40:16,191
I'm drowsy.

1154
00:40:18,591 --> 00:40:21,130
(He calls someone after finishing his meal.)

1155
00:40:21,131 --> 00:40:22,191
Hello.

1156
00:40:22,861 --> 00:40:23,961
Hello. What is it?

1157
00:40:24,401 --> 00:40:25,461
- It's his mom. - It's his mom.

1158
00:40:25,701 --> 00:40:26,701
What?

1159
00:40:26,702 --> 00:40:27,831
Where are you?

1160
00:40:28,401 --> 00:40:29,500
- Hello? - I'm in the neighborhood.

1161
00:40:29,501 --> 00:40:31,571
- Are you in the neighborhood? - Yes. Why?

1162
00:40:31,671 --> 00:40:33,970
- Today... - Today?

1163
00:40:33,971 --> 00:40:36,281
- Today, I visited Gimpo... - Okay.

1164
00:40:36,641 --> 00:40:38,941
(Burping)

1165
00:40:39,281 --> 00:40:41,380
Why are you burping so much while talking to your mom?

1166
00:40:41,381 --> 00:40:42,680
It just came out.

1167
00:40:42,681 --> 00:40:44,820
You could've called her after you were done.

1168
00:40:44,821 --> 00:40:46,121
- I didn't want to forget. - Okay.

1169
00:40:46,691 --> 00:40:50,021
I checked out some townhouses.

1170
00:40:50,061 --> 00:40:51,160
Okay.

1171
00:40:51,161 --> 00:40:53,490
- For goodness' sake. - I plan to rent out...

1172
00:40:53,491 --> 00:40:55,861
- my apartment in Samseong-dong. - Okay.

1173
00:40:56,061 --> 00:40:58,530
I'm worried since you're forgetful these days.

1174
00:40:58,531 --> 00:40:59,570
Okay.

1175
00:40:59,571 --> 00:41:02,071
I'm thinking about moving to Gimpo. What do you think about that?

1176
00:41:03,171 --> 00:41:04,900
- Us? - Are you telling her now?

1177
00:41:04,901 --> 00:41:06,440
- Didn't you tell her before? - No, I didn't.

1178
00:41:06,441 --> 00:41:09,141
It was a surprise. Had I told her, she would've been against it.

1179
00:41:09,741 --> 00:41:11,880
So, I wanted to tell her once things had progressed somewhat.

1180
00:41:11,881 --> 00:41:12,981
- Is that so? - Yes.

1181
00:41:13,611 --> 00:41:16,081
I'm thinking about moving to Gimpo. What do you think about that?

1182
00:41:17,221 --> 00:41:18,851
- Us? - Me.

1183
00:41:19,051 --> 00:41:20,821
You want to move to Gimpo?

1184
00:41:21,021 --> 00:41:22,050
What do you think about that?

1185
00:41:22,051 --> 00:41:24,591
I'll be 30 minutes away from your place.

1186
00:41:25,821 --> 00:41:27,060
It'll be nice.

1187
00:41:27,061 --> 00:41:28,160
Will it be nice?

1188
00:41:28,161 --> 00:41:29,360
It'll be nice.

1189
00:41:29,361 --> 00:41:30,430
Will it be nice?

1190
00:41:30,431 --> 00:41:32,201
I was surprised because it was an unexpected answer.

1191
00:41:32,561 --> 00:41:34,931
It'll be the best for us.

1192
00:41:35,101 --> 00:41:38,171
It'll be reassuring to have you around.

1193
00:41:38,871 --> 00:41:41,111
How does the place look?

1194
00:41:41,811 --> 00:41:42,911
It looks handsome.

1195
00:41:43,511 --> 00:41:44,580
Handsome?

1196
00:41:44,581 --> 00:41:46,280
I'll need to look into it more.

1197
00:41:46,281 --> 00:41:49,051
So you aren't against me moving to Gimpo, right?

1198
00:41:49,651 --> 00:41:53,020
I'm not against it, but it might be hard on you.

1199
00:41:53,021 --> 00:41:54,051
It'll be hard on me.

1200
00:41:54,421 --> 00:41:55,691
I'm doing this for you.

1201
00:41:56,621 --> 00:41:57,861
- Is that so? - Yes.

1202
00:41:59,261 --> 00:42:01,730
If it's hard on you, I'm not sure about it.

1203
00:42:01,731 --> 00:42:04,061
- You... - It won't benefit me.

1204
00:42:04,661 --> 00:42:06,970
- Then you shouldn't do it. - It'll be hard on me,

1205
00:42:06,971 --> 00:42:08,931
but it'll be okay since the TV stations are...

1206
00:42:09,331 --> 00:42:11,501
in Sangam-dong and Yeouido.

1207
00:42:11,671 --> 00:42:12,940
No, don't do it.

1208
00:42:12,941 --> 00:42:17,540
You should stay there. We'll travel to see you.

1209
00:42:17,541 --> 00:42:19,511
She changed her word since I said that it'd be hard on me.

1210
00:42:19,851 --> 00:42:21,650
Why did you boast about it?

1211
00:42:21,651 --> 00:42:23,881
You shouldn't tell your mom things like, "This is expensive."

1212
00:42:23,981 --> 00:42:25,280
"I went through much trouble to get it."

1213
00:42:25,281 --> 00:42:26,450
Moms don't like that.

1214
00:42:26,451 --> 00:42:28,691
I regretted making that comment.

1215
00:42:29,291 --> 00:42:30,521
I was like, "Why did I say that?"

1216
00:42:30,861 --> 00:42:32,461
I think she's actually happy about it.

1217
00:42:33,391 --> 00:42:35,730
- Seriously. - If you don't come to my place...

1218
00:42:35,731 --> 00:42:36,901
at times...

1219
00:42:37,361 --> 00:42:39,260
to do the dirty dishes and vacuum the floor,

1220
00:42:39,261 --> 00:42:41,170
I won't need to do this.

1221
00:42:41,171 --> 00:42:43,670
But you come to my place even when I tell you not to.

1222
00:42:43,671 --> 00:42:45,770
- My place is too far, - You regretted making that comment.

1223
00:42:45,771 --> 00:42:48,241
So I feel bad about you traveling all the way there.

1224
00:42:49,111 --> 00:42:51,881
- You just have to do those things. - No. That's...

1225
00:42:52,341 --> 00:42:55,180
We feel comfortable when we see traces of you.

1226
00:42:55,181 --> 00:42:56,921
When we're by ourselves,

1227
00:42:57,121 --> 00:42:58,980
we feel like we're at a Buddhist temple.

1228
00:42:58,981 --> 00:43:01,320
So, don't feel bad about my visits.

1229
00:43:01,321 --> 00:43:04,561
If you move to Gimpo, the long commute will wear you down.

1230
00:43:04,761 --> 00:43:06,491
- You need to think about that. - In any case,

1231
00:43:06,831 --> 00:43:08,661
I take it that you're okay with the idea.

1232
00:43:09,131 --> 00:43:10,300
- You're okay... - I'm not okay with the idea.

1233
00:43:10,301 --> 00:43:11,600
- No. - It won't be hard on me.

1234
00:43:11,601 --> 00:43:13,971
I want to try living in a townhouse.

1235
00:43:14,031 --> 00:43:15,370
Be quiet.

1236
00:43:15,371 --> 00:43:16,840
- I'll grow chili peppers. - Stop spouting nonsense.

1237
00:43:16,841 --> 00:43:18,201
Don't move to Gimpo.

1238
00:43:19,071 --> 00:43:20,071
Hello?

1239
00:43:20,941 --> 00:43:22,741
Why did I tell her that it'd be hard on me?

1240
00:43:24,041 --> 00:43:26,250
Firstly, I'll look more into the house in Gimpo...

1241
00:43:26,251 --> 00:43:28,451
I'll check it out more today with my real estate agent.

1242
00:43:28,811 --> 00:43:30,421
I'll talk to my mom more.

1243
00:43:30,751 --> 00:43:32,751
If she's really against me moving to Gimpo,

1244
00:43:33,291 --> 00:43:35,421
I could move her to that house.

1245
00:43:35,621 --> 00:43:37,760
I'll need to think about different ideas.

1246
00:43:37,761 --> 00:43:40,191
I'll need to take a careful approach for this project of filial duty.

1247
00:43:40,931 --> 00:43:43,131
She has made so many sacrifices in her life.

1248
00:43:43,231 --> 00:43:44,560
I don't want to think about me.

1249
00:43:44,561 --> 00:43:47,531
I want her to be a selfish mom who only thinks about herself.

1250
00:43:47,671 --> 00:43:50,070
Your life should be centered around you,

1251
00:43:50,071 --> 00:43:52,071
not us.

1252
00:43:52,271 --> 00:43:53,570
- You need to build your life. - Even if I move to Gimpo,

1253
00:43:53,571 --> 00:43:54,871
my life will be centered around me.

1254
00:43:55,241 --> 00:43:57,181
While I know that,

1255
00:43:57,441 --> 00:43:58,980
you need to get married. I'm against it.

1256
00:43:58,981 --> 00:44:01,851
- In any case, stay there. - Is marriage impossible in Gimpo?

1257
00:44:01,981 --> 00:44:04,580
Don't sell your current house. Since you became successful there,

1258
00:44:04,581 --> 00:44:06,081
you should hold on to it.

1259
00:44:06,291 --> 00:44:08,951
I won't decide today. In any case, I'll show you some properties.

1260
00:44:09,151 --> 00:44:10,461
Be quiet.

1261
00:44:10,691 --> 00:44:12,021
You aren't getting married.

1262
00:44:12,491 --> 00:44:15,131
- Be quiet. Then... - All right.

1263
00:44:15,491 --> 00:44:16,701
Don't get hurt.

1264
00:44:17,401 --> 00:44:19,431
- Okay. - She always says, "Don't get hurt."

1265
00:44:20,471 --> 00:44:21,631
Gosh.

1266
00:44:22,531 --> 00:44:24,701
I'm getting an upset stomach.

1267
00:44:26,971 --> 00:44:29,340
I'm getting an upset stomach because of Mom.

1268
00:44:29,341 --> 00:44:30,641
(The 47 Year Old Who Is Still Childish)

1269
00:44:31,041 --> 00:44:33,180
- I think that's filial love. - Really?

1270
00:44:33,181 --> 00:44:36,210
- Same here. - You usually don't keep in touch.

1271
00:44:36,211 --> 00:44:40,551
Talking about that is filial love.

1272
00:44:40,691 --> 00:44:41,791
You're right.

1273
00:44:42,021 --> 00:44:45,291
Then say a few words to your mom.

1274
00:44:45,591 --> 00:44:47,160
(Well...)

1275
00:44:47,161 --> 00:44:48,291
Firstly,

1276
00:44:49,391 --> 00:44:52,731
I didn't mean anything when I said that it'd be hard on me.

1277
00:44:53,101 --> 00:44:56,371
I've been dreaming of living in a place like that,

1278
00:44:56,771 --> 00:44:59,001
so please know that I'm doing this for myself.

1279
00:44:59,471 --> 00:45:01,340
- That's right. - Since you live nearby,

1280
00:45:01,341 --> 00:45:02,411
it's like killing 2 birds with 1 stone.

1281
00:45:02,671 --> 00:45:05,240
I'm not sacrificing myself for you and Dad.

1282
00:45:05,241 --> 00:45:07,310
Please understand that.

1283
00:45:07,311 --> 00:45:08,781
I'm not saying this for your sake.

1284
00:45:09,151 --> 00:45:10,151
- That's right. - Why didn't you say that...

1285
00:45:10,151 --> 00:45:11,151
on the phone?

1286
00:45:11,152 --> 00:45:12,280
- That's right. - That's right.

1287
00:45:12,281 --> 00:45:14,951
Hyun Moo, tell her that you love her.

1288
00:45:15,451 --> 00:45:17,060
- No. - Say it.

1289
00:45:17,061 --> 00:45:18,121
"I love you."

1290
00:45:19,321 --> 00:45:21,060
My mom will be uncomfortable.

1291
00:45:21,061 --> 00:45:23,401
- Why would she be uncomfortable? - Shall I say it in your stead?

1292
00:45:24,061 --> 00:45:25,461
- Shall I say it in your stead? - You should say it.

1293
00:45:26,901 --> 00:45:30,200
Ma'am, Hyun Moo loves you.

1294
00:45:30,201 --> 00:45:31,670
- What's this? - He loves you.

1295
00:45:31,671 --> 00:45:32,870
Even I feel embarrassed.

1296
00:45:32,871 --> 00:45:34,610
Tell your mom that you love her.

1297
00:45:34,611 --> 00:45:35,741
I can't do it.

1298
00:45:36,041 --> 00:45:37,440
- See? - Say it in his stead.

1299
00:45:37,441 --> 00:45:38,510
- Say it in his stead. - I can't do it.

1300
00:45:38,511 --> 00:45:40,980
Kian84's mom, Kian84 loves you as always.

1301
00:45:40,981 --> 00:45:42,281
- Oh, my. - What's this?

1302
00:45:42,481 --> 00:45:44,520
- Kian84 loves you. - What's this?

1303
00:45:44,521 --> 00:45:45,581
Please stay healthy.

1304
00:45:47,051 --> 00:45:49,190
Ko Kang Yong, welcome.

1305
00:45:49,191 --> 00:45:51,160
- It has been a while. - Hello.

1306
00:45:51,161 --> 00:45:52,190
- It has been a while. - My goodness.

1307
00:45:52,191 --> 00:45:54,060
Isn't it the 1st meeting for the 2 of you?

1308
00:45:54,061 --> 00:45:55,590
- Kang Yong and MINHO. - It's nice to meet you.

1309
00:45:55,591 --> 00:45:58,400
I watched your episode. It's our first time meeting.

1310
00:45:58,401 --> 00:46:00,300
I watched your episode too.

1311
00:46:00,301 --> 00:46:02,000
I thought we were similar in many ways.

1312
00:46:02,001 --> 00:46:03,140
In what ways?

1313
00:46:03,141 --> 00:46:06,610
There's alertness in his eyes.

1314
00:46:06,611 --> 00:46:08,071
It's natural to go overboard at that stage in his career.

1315
00:46:09,981 --> 00:46:12,111
While ramyeon was cooking,

1316
00:46:12,381 --> 00:46:13,881
- you took a shower. - Yes.

1317
00:46:14,851 --> 00:46:17,681
(MINHO's passionate ramyeon challenge)

1318
00:46:17,981 --> 00:46:19,721
After a workout,

1319
00:46:20,291 --> 00:46:22,021
I thaw a pack of chicken breast...

1320
00:46:22,251 --> 00:46:25,291
while taking a shower. I do it at times.

1321
00:46:25,861 --> 00:46:28,231
- Some people live like this. - That's right.

1322
00:46:28,431 --> 00:46:30,400
It's one of the traits that's shown by people...

1323
00:46:30,401 --> 00:46:32,160
who work out early in the morning.

1324
00:46:32,161 --> 00:46:33,530
(For goodness' sake)

1325
00:46:33,531 --> 00:46:34,901
- I have good news. - What is it?

1326
00:46:35,101 --> 00:46:36,901
- His solo album came out. - My goodness.

1327
00:46:37,741 --> 00:46:39,270
It came out after three years.

1328
00:46:39,271 --> 00:46:40,940
- That's impressive. - It came out.

1329
00:46:40,941 --> 00:46:42,211
You're preparing for solo promotions.

1330
00:46:42,441 --> 00:46:44,810
The album came out already.

1331
00:46:44,811 --> 00:46:47,581
- It came out today. - It came out today.

1332
00:46:47,681 --> 00:46:49,510
- Okay. - The music video got released.

1333
00:46:49,511 --> 00:46:51,620
- Give us the title. - It's "HUNTER."

1334
00:46:51,621 --> 00:46:52,950
- "HUNTER." - "HUNTER."

1335
00:46:52,951 --> 00:46:54,491
- It's an intense title. - I like it.

1336
00:46:55,121 --> 00:46:57,420
(Will You Recharge Yourself?)

1337
00:46:57,421 --> 00:46:58,861
"Will You Recharge Yourself?"

1338
00:47:02,061 --> 00:47:04,101
It looks like he's enveloped in a blanket.

1339
00:47:05,361 --> 00:47:07,401
(It's quiet inside the room.)

1340
00:47:08,031 --> 00:47:09,841
(Kang Yong is recharging his energy.)

1341
00:47:10,871 --> 00:47:12,670
Do you like PSG? Are you a PSG fan?

1342
00:47:12,671 --> 00:47:14,840
- I went to France. - I see.

1343
00:47:14,841 --> 00:47:16,310
As I was buying Lee Kang In's uniform,

1344
00:47:16,311 --> 00:47:17,311
- I decided to get that too. - How did you know that?

1345
00:47:17,311 --> 00:47:18,311
Where does it say that?

1346
00:47:18,311 --> 00:47:19,311
It's next to Wilson.

1347
00:47:19,312 --> 00:47:20,581
- It's next to Wilson. - I see.

1348
00:47:20,811 --> 00:47:22,110
- Wasn't that the logo for Pepsi? - No.

1349
00:47:22,111 --> 00:47:24,420
That's the logo for Paris Saint-Germain F.C.

1350
00:47:24,421 --> 00:47:26,691
- That was seen as Pepsi? - Wasn't it Domino's Pizza?

1351
00:47:26,851 --> 00:47:28,421
Wasn't that the box for Domino's Pizza?

1352
00:47:28,491 --> 00:47:30,721
Only CODE KUNST, MINHO, and I noticed it.

1353
00:47:30,821 --> 00:47:32,621
- I see. - Just the soccer fans.

1354
00:47:34,361 --> 00:47:36,090
- Aren't you just a human fan? - Human fan?

1355
00:47:36,091 --> 00:47:37,461
Human fan.

1356
00:47:38,431 --> 00:47:40,971
(Kang Yong is still in dreamland.)

1357
00:47:42,001 --> 00:47:43,770
So this place doesn't have blackout curtains.

1358
00:47:43,771 --> 00:47:45,640
- Right. - I didn't think I could wake up...

1359
00:47:45,641 --> 00:47:47,110
with blackout curtains.

1360
00:47:47,111 --> 00:47:48,270
- I couldn't put them up. - There are people like that.

1361
00:47:48,271 --> 00:47:49,311
Right.

1362
00:47:49,771 --> 00:47:53,211
(He was able to get up due to the lack of blackout curtains.)

1363
00:47:57,121 --> 00:47:59,721
Hello. I'm MBC's announcer, Ko Kang Yong.

1364
00:47:59,851 --> 00:48:01,490
Announcer Ko Kang Yong.

1365
00:48:01,491 --> 00:48:05,091
(MBC's rookie announcer that has entered less than a year ago)

1366
00:48:05,561 --> 00:48:06,561
(Hello.)

1367
00:48:06,562 --> 00:48:08,530
(Passionate as a rookie)

1368
00:48:08,531 --> 00:48:09,591
(Hello.)

1369
00:48:10,201 --> 00:48:11,701
(And...)

1370
00:48:12,401 --> 00:48:14,471
(his down-to-earth home got a lot of attention.)

1371
00:48:14,501 --> 00:48:16,171
It's an old house.

1372
00:48:16,231 --> 00:48:17,340
(He was like a relatable friend. I wish to see more of him.)

1373
00:48:17,341 --> 00:48:18,500
(It was interesting to watch as it was realistic.)

1374
00:48:18,501 --> 00:48:19,800
(Relatable as a K-Office Worker)

1375
00:48:19,801 --> 00:48:22,011
- A lot of people felt sympathy. - Right.

1376
00:48:22,541 --> 00:48:24,141
How was it after being on the show?

1377
00:48:24,281 --> 00:48:26,750
First of all, a lot of people recognized me.

1378
00:48:26,751 --> 00:48:30,321
I went to a kalguksu place and the old lady owner...

1379
00:48:30,781 --> 00:48:32,550
kept asking if I was the one on I Live Alone.

1380
00:48:32,551 --> 00:48:34,351
- She even gave me free dumplings. - My gosh!

1381
00:48:34,521 --> 00:48:35,620
Free dumplings mean so much.

1382
00:48:35,621 --> 00:48:37,420
- She kept telling me to come back. - Gosh, dumplings?

1383
00:48:37,421 --> 00:48:39,121
I gave a lot of autographs too.

1384
00:48:39,421 --> 00:48:40,730
After being on I Live Alone,

1385
00:48:40,731 --> 00:48:43,831
my parents changed their profile pictures...

1386
00:48:43,861 --> 00:48:45,560
to a scene from my appearance on the show.

1387
00:48:45,561 --> 00:48:46,971
(His mother's actual profile)

1388
00:48:47,131 --> 00:48:48,470
This is what my mother did.

1389
00:48:48,471 --> 00:48:50,971
Reruns of the show are shown every day throughout the week.

1390
00:48:51,001 --> 00:48:53,070
- Right. - She watched all of the reruns.

1391
00:48:53,071 --> 00:48:54,170
My goodness.

1392
00:48:54,171 --> 00:48:56,541
- That isn't easy to do. - That isn't easy to do.

1393
00:48:56,941 --> 00:48:59,310
"Why write so much in your journal as a young man?"

1394
00:48:59,311 --> 00:49:00,681
I got a lot of attention from the people around me.

1395
00:49:01,051 --> 00:49:03,721
(He got busier as he gained more attention these days.)

1396
00:49:04,321 --> 00:49:06,551
(Unlike the busy times he had these days, )

1397
00:49:07,021 --> 00:49:09,961
(Is Kang Yong enjoying some free time in bed?)

1398
00:49:10,491 --> 00:49:12,820
It was my day off after a while.

1399
00:49:12,821 --> 00:49:14,060
It was Saturday,

1400
00:49:14,061 --> 00:49:15,561
so I didn't set the alarm.

1401
00:49:15,661 --> 00:49:18,061
I allowed myself to sleep until my eyes opened.

1402
00:49:18,231 --> 00:49:20,031
No wonder you looked relaxed.

1403
00:49:20,971 --> 00:49:22,670
I usually woke up to the alarm on weekdays.

1404
00:49:22,671 --> 00:49:24,401
(He worked too hard in the weekdays.)

1405
00:49:24,801 --> 00:49:27,641
I wanted to be free from the alarm at least during the weekends.

1406
00:49:28,371 --> 00:49:31,380
There are times when my eyes open even without the alarm.

1407
00:49:31,381 --> 00:49:32,410
I feel really happy when I get back to sleep...

1408
00:49:32,411 --> 00:49:33,480
after knowing it's the weekend.

1409
00:49:33,481 --> 00:49:35,351
- Gosh, that's the best feeling. - That's the best feeling.

1410
00:49:35,581 --> 00:49:36,920
This happened when I was an announcer.

1411
00:49:36,921 --> 00:49:38,250
- It's dark in the winter. - Right.

1412
00:49:38,251 --> 00:49:40,721
I used to be on a radio show that was at dawn.

1413
00:49:41,421 --> 00:49:43,290
I opened my eyes...

1414
00:49:43,291 --> 00:49:45,461
and it was really bright. It felt like it was 9am.

1415
00:49:45,691 --> 00:49:46,831
I cried.

1416
00:49:47,691 --> 00:49:48,791
I cried like this.

1417
00:49:49,931 --> 00:49:51,660
- I cried. - You couldn't do anything...

1418
00:49:51,661 --> 00:49:53,000
and you thought you were in big trouble.

1419
00:49:53,001 --> 00:49:54,430
- I couldn't look at my phone. - Right.

1420
00:49:54,431 --> 00:49:56,031
I just wept right away.

1421
00:49:57,071 --> 00:49:58,601
I did this after waking up with no clothes on.

1422
00:50:00,141 --> 00:50:02,211
He has a lot of body heat.

1423
00:50:02,541 --> 00:50:03,640
It was a Saturday though.

1424
00:50:03,641 --> 00:50:05,180
- There are those moments. - You know what I mean, right?

1425
00:50:05,181 --> 00:50:06,650
- I definitely know what you mean. - That must've woken you up.

1426
00:50:06,651 --> 00:50:08,081
- Office workers go through this. - Right.

1427
00:50:09,211 --> 00:50:11,781
(Current time: 10:09am)

1428
00:50:12,421 --> 00:50:13,450
(He watches baseball in bed.)

1429
00:50:13,451 --> 00:50:14,891
It must be nice to have a day off.

1430
00:50:16,691 --> 00:50:17,960
I'm like that too.

1431
00:50:17,961 --> 00:50:19,560
I always watch sports highlights too.

1432
00:50:19,561 --> 00:50:20,730
MINHO is amazing at baseball.

1433
00:50:20,731 --> 00:50:22,791
(MINHO is amazing at baseball.)

1434
00:50:25,061 --> 00:50:26,460
(Let's get up and tidy things up.)

1435
00:50:26,461 --> 00:50:28,371
You could just leave it alone as it's the weekend.

1436
00:50:29,801 --> 00:50:32,971
(He diligently tidies up the bedding even on the weekend.)

1437
00:50:35,841 --> 00:50:36,941
(Grabbing)

1438
00:50:39,411 --> 00:50:41,081
(He sets up the table.)

1439
00:50:44,981 --> 00:50:47,951
(Let's eat first.)

1440
00:50:51,891 --> 00:50:53,320
That's the glutinous rice sent from my mother.

1441
00:50:53,321 --> 00:50:54,691
She continues to send some over to me.

1442
00:50:58,901 --> 00:51:00,701
The egg jangjorim must taste really good.

1443
00:51:02,001 --> 00:51:03,570
(When the side dishes get heated up, )

1444
00:51:03,571 --> 00:51:04,571
Is it done?

1445
00:51:05,701 --> 00:51:07,510
(a breakfast meal is ready right away.)

1446
00:51:07,511 --> 00:51:08,911
- That looks good. - That looks good.

1447
00:51:10,211 --> 00:51:11,411
- What is that? - What is that?

1448
00:51:11,641 --> 00:51:12,781
What is that?

1449
00:51:13,011 --> 00:51:14,080
It's braised skate.

1450
00:51:14,081 --> 00:51:15,351
- Braised skate? - Braised skate?

1451
00:51:15,951 --> 00:51:17,220
(Thank you, Mother.)

1452
00:51:17,221 --> 00:51:18,750
She sends a lot of precious dishes.

1453
00:51:18,751 --> 00:51:20,191
She sends a lot of food.

1454
00:51:25,921 --> 00:51:27,560
- Braised skate is really good. - Braised skate?

1455
00:51:27,561 --> 00:51:29,390
- Right. - Have you tried braised skate?

1456
00:51:29,391 --> 00:51:30,900
- I've never tried it. - I've never seen it before.

1457
00:51:30,901 --> 00:51:32,560
- It's my first time seeing it. - It's really good.

1458
00:51:32,561 --> 00:51:33,831
It's good. It tastes clean.

1459
00:51:35,631 --> 00:51:37,441
(Relaxed)

1460
00:51:38,171 --> 00:51:41,741
(Unlike how he shoved in his food during the weekdays, )

1461
00:51:43,481 --> 00:51:44,980
(he looks peaceful during the weekend.)

1462
00:51:44,981 --> 00:51:46,751
This is the best thing about weekends.

1463
00:51:49,751 --> 00:51:52,281
(After enjoying the food in peace, )

1464
00:51:53,721 --> 00:51:55,721
(the bowls get emptied.)

1465
00:51:57,361 --> 00:52:00,461
(Let's clean up right away.)

1466
00:52:02,031 --> 00:52:04,961
(Groaning)

1467
00:52:07,901 --> 00:52:09,271
There's a big pile.

1468
00:52:09,471 --> 00:52:12,241
As I was busy during the weekdays,

1469
00:52:12,601 --> 00:52:16,441
I usually did the dishes all at once during the weekends.

1470
00:52:16,511 --> 00:52:18,480
There must've been around five pairs of chopsticks.

1471
00:52:18,481 --> 00:52:20,381
I wasn't able to take care of the dishes at all.

1472
00:52:21,511 --> 00:52:26,251
(Let's wash them as it's the weekend.)

1473
00:52:28,091 --> 00:52:30,921
(He washes the chopsticks piled up during the weekdays.)

1474
00:52:32,421 --> 00:52:33,561
Gosh, there are fruit flies.

1475
00:52:35,331 --> 00:52:36,690
(He even has a fruit fly trap set up.)

1476
00:52:36,691 --> 00:52:38,501
Gosh, those darn fruit flies.

1477
00:52:39,901 --> 00:52:42,471
(Washing with his bare hands)

1478
00:52:44,101 --> 00:52:46,871
(He thoroughly tries to dry up the water around the sink.)

1479
00:52:48,011 --> 00:52:49,711
(Grabbing)

1480
00:52:50,381 --> 00:52:51,910
(Sniffing)

1481
00:52:51,911 --> 00:52:52,941
The laundry?

1482
00:52:53,551 --> 00:52:56,011
I was just going to wash the towel,

1483
00:52:56,311 --> 00:52:58,520
but I could see the things that need to be washed.

1484
00:52:58,521 --> 00:53:00,690
You always find them after you start washing them.

1485
00:53:00,691 --> 00:53:01,821
- Right. - Right.

1486
00:53:02,121 --> 00:53:03,620
- There are those times. - Gosh.

1487
00:53:03,621 --> 00:53:04,721
They have to be done at once.

1488
00:53:05,591 --> 00:53:09,191
(Current time: 10:57am)

1489
00:53:09,391 --> 00:53:11,101
(Thinking)

1490
00:53:11,161 --> 00:53:12,701
Gosh, I should take this off.

1491
00:53:15,731 --> 00:53:17,770
- What is that? - It's newspaper.

1492
00:53:17,771 --> 00:53:19,741
- It's to block the oil. - The oil?

1493
00:53:19,841 --> 00:53:22,371
I flip fried eggs often.

1494
00:53:22,671 --> 00:53:24,341
I flip them without using a spatula.

1495
00:53:24,711 --> 00:53:26,210
That is when the oil splatters.

1496
00:53:26,211 --> 00:53:27,410
Gosh, look at the frying pan.

1497
00:53:27,411 --> 00:53:29,951
(The oily items are moved.)

1498
00:53:30,051 --> 00:53:31,781
(Thinking)

1499
00:53:35,551 --> 00:53:37,021
It has the looks of an old restaurant.

1500
00:53:37,321 --> 00:53:38,461
Right.

1501
00:53:38,621 --> 00:53:39,860
- This wasn't an old restaurant? - Do you clean your place...

1502
00:53:39,861 --> 00:53:41,091
every single day?

1503
00:53:41,961 --> 00:53:44,530
This is quite clean in my standards.

1504
00:53:44,531 --> 00:53:46,001
(This is quite clean in my standards.)

1505
00:53:46,161 --> 00:53:48,101
(Snickering)

1506
00:53:48,171 --> 00:53:49,830
- That's clean? - It's not that clean...

1507
00:53:49,831 --> 00:53:50,971
after looking at it closely.

1508
00:53:51,341 --> 00:53:52,901
(Tearing up)

1509
00:53:54,541 --> 00:53:57,481
(He sprays the detergent to make it clean.)

1510
00:53:59,341 --> 00:54:01,080
(Spraying a generous amount)

1511
00:54:01,081 --> 00:54:02,311
That's a tough stain.

1512
00:54:02,751 --> 00:54:04,320
I push it back and avoid it,

1513
00:54:04,321 --> 00:54:06,351
but there are times when it bothers me.

1514
00:54:06,621 --> 00:54:07,821
Let's see.

1515
00:54:08,391 --> 00:54:09,990
Rubber gloves? I don't have any.

