1775
01:04:12,921 --> 01:04:14,261
I think he's going pretty far away.

1776
01:04:14,931 --> 01:04:16,231
Is he going to meet his parents?

1777
01:04:16,691 --> 01:04:17,860
He's in Gyeonggi Province.

1778
01:04:17,861 --> 01:04:19,400
(Past Seoul)

1779
01:04:19,401 --> 01:04:21,131
He's going far away. He's going all the way to Suwon?

1780
01:04:22,071 --> 01:04:24,841
I will be working on my commentating at the baseball stadium.

1781
01:04:25,141 --> 01:04:26,840
That is why I'm heading to Suwon.

1782
01:04:26,841 --> 01:04:28,841
(That is why I'm heading to Suwon.)

1783
01:04:30,641 --> 01:04:32,381
I'm almost there.

1784
01:04:34,251 --> 01:04:36,211
(This place...)

1785
01:04:36,981 --> 01:04:38,420
(is Suwon Wiz Park.)

1786
01:04:38,421 --> 01:04:39,981
It's Suwon Wiz Park.

1787
01:04:40,651 --> 01:04:42,491
(Professional baseball is at its peak right now.)

1788
01:04:43,121 --> 01:04:44,520
("Professional Baseball Reaches 9 Million Visitors in 528 Games")

1789
01:04:44,521 --> 01:04:45,861
("New Sales Record in 2025 with 224 Games Filled")

1790
01:04:46,721 --> 01:04:48,260
It was really hot that day.

1791
01:04:48,261 --> 01:04:49,430
Fans go to watch even when it's over 40°C.

1792
01:04:49,431 --> 01:04:50,690
No one can stop their passion.

1793
01:04:50,691 --> 01:04:52,561
(The lively sight of competition)

1794
01:04:53,831 --> 01:04:56,471
(It's a breathtaking sight.)

1795
01:04:58,241 --> 01:05:00,641
(He arrives at the baseball stadium.)

1796
01:05:05,441 --> 01:05:07,551
Will he practice on his own then?

1797
01:05:07,811 --> 01:05:10,551
- Won't there be someone to help? - Won't there be someone with him?

1798
01:05:11,251 --> 01:05:12,720
Gosh, it's so hot.

1799
01:05:12,721 --> 01:05:13,881
There must be someone there.

1800
01:05:15,091 --> 01:05:16,290
(He calls someone while taking in the sunlight fully.)

1801
01:05:16,291 --> 01:05:17,761
Where are you right now, sir?

1802
01:05:18,721 --> 01:05:19,990
Do you see the Samsung team buses?

1803
01:05:19,991 --> 01:05:21,760
Yes. I see three of them.

1804
01:05:21,761 --> 01:05:23,990
Around the team bus...

1805
01:05:23,991 --> 01:05:26,461
I think it's the one that helped Dae Ho.

1806
01:05:27,431 --> 01:05:29,471
- I'll see you there. - Okay. I'll be there.

1807
01:05:30,631 --> 01:05:33,041
(He feels the heat of the baseball stadium up close.)

1808
01:05:33,801 --> 01:05:35,611
(His heart starts beating at the thought of commentating.)

1809
01:05:36,841 --> 01:05:39,080
(Looking around)

1810
01:05:39,081 --> 01:05:40,111
Oh, right.

1811
01:05:40,881 --> 01:05:42,451
Sir!

1812
01:05:43,381 --> 01:05:44,551
You're here, Kang Yong.

1813
01:05:44,851 --> 01:05:46,051
- The angel? - It's him.

1814
01:05:46,451 --> 01:05:48,450
- It's Announcer Kim Na Jin. - Right.

1815
01:05:48,451 --> 01:05:50,221
- Dae Ho's savior. - The angel announcer.

1816
01:05:52,191 --> 01:05:55,030
(Dae Ho's savior who taught Dae Ho in Paris)

1817
01:05:55,031 --> 01:05:56,631
He's such a sweet guy.

1818
01:05:57,161 --> 01:05:59,731
(He also advises Kang Yong whenever he can.)

1819
01:05:59,931 --> 01:06:01,871
Right. I remember.

1820
01:06:02,331 --> 01:06:06,041
Senior Na Jin is a representative sportscaster of MBC.

1821
01:06:07,101 --> 01:06:08,470
(The all-round caster of all sports)

1822
01:06:08,471 --> 01:06:09,971
He can work with any sport.

1823
01:06:10,141 --> 01:06:12,310
The comments of sportscasters are really important too.

1824
01:06:12,311 --> 01:06:13,311
- Right. - Right.

1825
01:06:13,312 --> 01:06:14,781
When the Twins won the championship,

1826
01:06:15,351 --> 01:06:19,781
Na Jin made the fans emotional...

1827
01:06:20,121 --> 01:06:22,350
with his championship call.

1828
01:06:22,351 --> 01:06:23,391
What was it again?

1829
01:06:24,321 --> 01:06:26,420
(When the Twins won the championship in 2023)

1830
01:06:26,421 --> 01:06:28,430
The Twins won the championship in 29 years.

1831
01:06:28,431 --> 01:06:29,431
Right.

1832
01:06:29,432 --> 01:06:32,861
Who were you in fall of 1994?

1833
01:06:33,161 --> 01:06:36,331
And who are you now today?

1834
01:06:36,971 --> 01:06:38,670
("Korea Series Match 5 Championship Call Brings Tears")

1835
01:06:38,671 --> 01:06:40,341
("Fans Shed Tears After Hearing Commentator's Championship Call")

1836
01:06:40,541 --> 01:06:42,271
This is the live footage.

1837
01:06:42,411 --> 01:06:44,141
- Is there no script for that? - No.

1838
01:06:44,211 --> 01:06:46,380
- It's just written beforehand. - He prepared it beforehand.

1839
01:06:46,381 --> 01:06:48,781
- Right. - That comment is so impressive.

1840
01:06:49,281 --> 01:06:52,550
Recently, I was the sportscaster for College Basketball.

1841
01:06:52,551 --> 01:06:53,880
The Sangju competition.

1842
01:06:53,881 --> 01:06:56,621
(Kang Yong made his debut as a sportscaster.)

1843
01:06:57,251 --> 01:06:59,361
He watched the whole thing from start to finish...

1844
01:06:59,921 --> 01:07:02,191
