2027
01:13:12,182 --> 01:13:13,642
(Entering the broadcast van, following Na Jin)

2028
01:13:15,082 --> 01:13:17,681
(With cutting-edge broadcasting equipment...)

2029
01:13:17,682 --> 01:13:19,782
- How fascinating. - That's amazing.

2030
01:13:20,982 --> 01:13:23,892
It was almost like the sub-control room.

2031
01:13:24,022 --> 01:13:25,092
It was really fascinating.

2032
01:13:26,062 --> 01:13:29,262
(The sub-control room that oversees "MBC News Today")

2033
01:13:29,992 --> 01:13:31,832
It looks exactly like the sub-control room.

2034
01:13:32,762 --> 01:13:34,232
Sir, is it okay to bother you?

2035
01:13:34,332 --> 01:13:35,332
Yes.

2036
01:13:35,333 --> 01:13:36,371
Hello, I'm...

2037
01:13:36,372 --> 01:13:39,001
- I'm MBC Announcer, Ko Kang Yong. - He's the new announcer, Kang Yong.

2038
01:13:39,002 --> 01:13:40,002
Nice to meet you.

2039
01:13:40,003 --> 01:13:42,171
- Na Jin got this drink. - He prepared...

2040
01:13:42,172 --> 01:13:43,472
- Gosh, he got you this. - Thank you.

2041
01:13:43,842 --> 01:13:47,012
He's the chief manager of broadcasting.

2042
01:13:47,182 --> 01:13:48,812
He controls everything...

2043
01:13:48,952 --> 01:13:51,551
from cameras to equipment. He's the chief manager.

2044
01:13:51,552 --> 01:13:54,022
So ask him whatever you want.

2045
01:13:54,552 --> 01:13:55,921
Can you teach him...

2046
01:13:55,922 --> 01:13:58,861
- how to control the cameras? - Basically...

2047
01:13:58,862 --> 01:14:01,861
We numbered every camera, as you can see.

2048
01:14:01,862 --> 01:14:03,591
- Are there 12 in total? - We are using...

2049
01:14:03,592 --> 01:14:06,002
thirteen cameras.

2050
01:14:06,462 --> 01:14:08,902
What I do is go to certain cameras...

2051
01:14:09,632 --> 01:14:13,171
and decide which screen to show, like Camera 7 or Camera 8.

2052
01:14:13,172 --> 01:14:15,411
But there's no such thing as a rehearsal in sports.

2053
01:14:15,412 --> 01:14:17,712
So you shift to another camera while watching the screens.

2054
01:14:18,242 --> 01:14:20,982
Then the completed scenes are transmitted.

2055
01:14:21,342 --> 01:14:23,051
When Dae Ho shot water,

2056
01:14:23,052 --> 01:14:24,752
- did you prepare in advance? - We have it here.

2057
01:14:24,952 --> 01:14:26,821
- Where? You prepared in advance... - That's right.

2058
01:14:26,822 --> 01:14:27,882
Shot water?

2059
01:14:28,152 --> 01:14:29,692
What is that?

2060
01:14:30,192 --> 01:14:31,721
Over there. He was on screen all of a sudden.

2061
01:14:31,722 --> 01:14:33,221
A scene like that.

2062
01:14:33,222 --> 01:14:34,892
Dae Ho was at the stadium the day before.

2063
01:14:35,462 --> 01:14:38,461
- I thought he was busy. - What is he doing?

2064
01:14:38,462 --> 01:14:41,002
- He's shooting water there? - What is he doing there?

2065
01:14:41,362 --> 01:14:42,902
He's become really free.

2066
01:14:43,032 --> 01:14:44,172
He's too free.

2067
01:14:44,632 --> 01:14:45,942
He danced with cheerleaders too.

2068
01:14:46,202 --> 01:14:47,672
Oh, my goodness!

2069
01:14:48,312 --> 01:14:49,872
(Sexy)

2070
01:14:50,772 --> 01:14:53,142
(Dancing in sync)

2071
01:14:53,812 --> 01:14:55,351
He's become a middle-aged man.

2072
01:14:55,352 --> 01:14:57,452
- He does whatever he wants now. - It's embarrassing for us.

2073
01:14:58,452 --> 01:14:59,781
My former senior.

2074
01:14:59,782 --> 01:15:00,821
Since he left.

2075
01:15:00,822 --> 01:15:02,052
He looks so happy.

2076
01:15:02,322 --> 01:15:04,962
Is there something...

2077
01:15:05,222 --> 01:15:06,721
you wished sportscasters did?

2078
01:15:06,722 --> 01:15:08,962
What are some of the virtues of a sportscaster?

2079
01:15:09,432 --> 01:15:13,232
Sports broadcast producers...

2080
01:15:13,462 --> 01:15:16,132
create scenes that sportscasters want.

2081
01:15:17,372 --> 01:15:20,941
On the other hand, we also want the sportscasters...

2082
01:15:20,942 --> 01:15:22,842
to lead the comment to certain ways.

2083
01:15:23,112 --> 01:15:25,912
When we create scenes with such intention,

2084
01:15:26,042 --> 01:15:28,511
they must be able to catch what we want.

2085
01:15:28,512 --> 01:15:29,751
(They must be able to catch the producer's intention.)

2086
01:15:29,752 --> 01:15:31,721
So the editing and comments need to go hand in hand.

2087
01:15:31,722 --> 01:15:33,521
- Yes. - You should pick up on things fast.

2088
01:15:33,522 --> 01:15:35,852
- That's right, to match the scenes. - You need to be sensible.

2089
01:15:36,622 --> 01:15:37,892
You can see this, right?

2090
01:15:38,562 --> 01:15:39,692
That's right.

2091
01:15:39,822 --> 01:15:40,921
"Even if you live separately, you're still family."

2092
01:15:40,922 --> 01:15:42,092
"Even if you live separately, you're still family."

2093
01:15:42,692 --> 01:15:44,532
That kind of timing is also important.

2094
01:15:45,602 --> 01:15:47,531
- Thank you so much. - Thank you, sir.

2095
01:15:47,532 --> 01:15:48,532
(I'll keep that in mind.)

2096
01:15:48,772 --> 01:15:50,071
- Keep up the good work. - Yes, you too.

2097
01:15:50,072 --> 01:15:51,541
- Keep up the good work. - Thank you, sir.

2098
01:15:51,542 --> 01:15:52,572
Bye.

2099
01:15:54,172 --> 01:15:57,142
I secured an empty commentary booth.

2100
01:15:57,172 --> 01:15:59,482
Let's practice commentating...

2101
01:15:59,882 --> 01:16:01,342
while watching the game...

2102
01:16:01,442 --> 01:16:03,052
- and filling out record sheets. - Okay.

2103
01:16:04,612 --> 01:16:07,821
Na Jin secured a booth next to the commentary booth...

2104
01:16:07,822 --> 01:16:10,021
- of that day. - Just like actual broadcasting?

2105
01:16:10,022 --> 01:16:12,622
That's amazing. That's such a good experience.

2106
01:16:12,892 --> 01:16:14,622
(The two seniors are busy preparing for the broadcast.)

2107
01:16:14,992 --> 01:16:16,261
It feels different, right?

2108
01:16:16,262 --> 01:16:17,632
- It's really different. - Yes.

2109
01:16:18,162 --> 01:16:19,261
(Practicing like it's an actual broadcast)

2110
01:16:19,262 --> 01:16:20,461
It's really close.

2111
01:16:20,462 --> 01:16:21,601
- Did you bring record sheets? - Yes, I did.

2112
01:16:21,602 --> 01:16:23,302
- We need to take a look. - What are record sheets?

2113
01:16:25,772 --> 01:16:27,141
- Gosh. - What is that?

2114
01:16:27,142 --> 01:16:28,971
- Oh, it's from a previous game. - That's amazing.

2115
01:16:28,972 --> 01:16:30,711
For record sheets...

2116
01:16:30,712 --> 01:16:32,812
Write down the names of the players here.

2117
01:16:32,912 --> 01:16:35,112
- I differentiate them with colors. - I see.

2118
01:16:35,682 --> 01:16:38,112
Every sportscaster has a different way of writing.

2119
01:16:38,382 --> 01:16:39,781
He really is a veteran.

2120
01:16:39,782 --> 01:16:40,921
Gosh, that's impressive.

2121
01:16:40,922 --> 01:16:42,991
You need to bring out the things that you wrote down here.

2122
01:16:42,992 --> 01:16:44,792
(You can tell the charisma of the veteran from the sheet.)

2123
01:16:44,822 --> 01:16:48,261
Is it a record of players' participation...

2124
01:16:48,262 --> 01:16:51,231
- and their batting average? - Their records.

2125
01:16:51,232 --> 01:16:52,431
There's a separate record of that.

2126
01:16:52,432 --> 01:16:54,131
- What is this? - It's a record of the game.

2127
01:16:54,132 --> 01:16:56,601
If you look here, there's a list of hitters.

2128
01:16:56,602 --> 01:16:58,971
- And a list of innings. - Yes.

2129
01:16:58,972 --> 01:17:01,771
It's a record of whether there was a hit...

2130
01:17:01,772 --> 01:17:03,311
or a double in each inning.

2131
01:17:03,312 --> 01:17:04,941
- Or a 3-strikeout. - Or a 3-strikeout.

2132
01:17:04,942 --> 01:17:07,181
- He converted that into a symbol... - So it's easier to see.

2133
01:17:07,182 --> 01:17:08,812
And recorded it.

2134
01:17:08,952 --> 01:17:10,411
Today, we have Coach Park Jin Man.

2135
01:17:10,412 --> 01:17:13,021
I wrote down what he did and where,

2136
01:17:13,022 --> 01:17:14,821
and his coaching staff,

2137
01:17:14,822 --> 01:17:17,091
so it's easier to see.

2138
01:17:17,092 --> 01:17:18,661
Write down the coaching staff here.

2139
01:17:18,662 --> 01:17:21,991
You need to keep a record in your own style.

2140
01:17:21,992 --> 01:17:23,162
- I see. - Yes.

2141
01:17:23,632 --> 01:17:26,931
You need to memorize the information about the stadium.

2142
01:17:26,932 --> 01:17:28,672
- He's right. - This is so much fun.

2143
01:17:28,832 --> 01:17:30,572
What represents Suwon?

2144
01:17:31,302 --> 01:17:32,671
- Big galbi chicken. - The Hwaseong...

2145
01:17:32,672 --> 01:17:34,671
- Oh, it's the Hwaseong Fortress. - Yes, it's the Hwaseong Fortress.

2146
01:17:34,672 --> 01:17:35,711
He's right too.

2147
01:17:35,712 --> 01:17:37,412
- Such things... - Big galbi chicken is famous too.

2148
01:17:37,612 --> 01:17:38,841
Oh, it's the Hwaseong Fortress.

2149
01:17:38,842 --> 01:17:41,241
You need to know the history of that area too.

2150
01:17:41,242 --> 01:17:42,912
- You need to know a lot. - If you look here...

2151
01:17:43,412 --> 01:17:46,051
Add the Korea Meteorological Administration to shortcut.

2152
01:17:46,052 --> 01:17:47,152
To check the weather.

2153
01:17:47,622 --> 01:17:49,291
It includes the sunrise and sunset times.

2154
01:17:49,292 --> 01:17:50,421
- Okay. - Things like this.

2155
01:17:50,422 --> 01:17:52,392
You need to check the expected temperature.

2156
01:17:52,722 --> 01:17:54,761
Is it really possible to prepare all this?

2157
01:17:54,762 --> 01:17:56,331
You need to talk about such things too.

2158
01:17:56,332 --> 01:17:57,831
There are so many things to prepare.

2159
01:17:57,832 --> 01:17:58,932
That's right.

2160
01:17:59,062 --> 01:18:01,262
I watch baseball games a lot.

2161
01:18:01,532 --> 01:18:03,802
(A true baseball fan who always watches baseball games)

2162
01:18:04,272 --> 01:18:06,941
I'd hear the information that sportscasters share,

2163
01:18:06,942 --> 01:18:08,611
and I'd learn such information.

2164
01:18:08,612 --> 01:18:10,371
"Oh, that was why."

2165
01:18:10,372 --> 01:18:12,112
The sportscasters that share information...

2166
01:18:12,442 --> 01:18:14,081
- are really useful for the fans. - That's right.

2167
01:18:14,082 --> 01:18:16,581
There are no other sports games...

2168
01:18:16,582 --> 01:18:17,851
- that last this long. - That's right.

2169
01:18:17,852 --> 01:18:20,151
- Sportscasters need to speak a lot. - That's right.

2170
01:18:20,152 --> 01:18:22,021
There's nothing they can say if there are like ten foul balls.

2171
01:18:22,022 --> 01:18:23,551
- Then what should you do? - "What's wrong with him?"

2172
01:18:23,552 --> 01:18:24,652
You can't just say that.

2173
01:18:25,492 --> 01:18:27,891
- Right? It gets really boring. - That's right.

2174
01:18:27,892 --> 01:18:29,061
- Then what should you do? - You're right.

2175
01:18:29,062 --> 01:18:30,891
- You talk about such things. - You need to explain it.

2176
01:18:30,892 --> 01:18:32,901
- Yes, you need to explain. - Why the player hit a foul ball.

2177
01:18:32,902 --> 01:18:35,172
You need to be really creative.

2178
01:18:35,502 --> 01:18:38,132
(10 minutes before the game)

2179
01:18:38,842 --> 01:18:40,371
(The fans enter one by one.)

2180
01:18:40,372 --> 01:18:42,271
Gosh, this is like...

2181
01:18:42,272 --> 01:18:45,681
(Wiz versus Lions)

2182
01:18:45,682 --> 01:18:47,581
- It was packed. - In this weather?

2183
01:18:47,582 --> 01:18:49,412
Baseball stadiums are always packed.

2184
01:18:51,682 --> 01:18:53,882
(The broadcasting starts as well.)

2185
01:18:54,482 --> 01:18:56,892
(Super nervous)

2186
01:18:57,692 --> 01:19:00,562
(It begins now.)

2187
01:19:00,762 --> 01:19:04,531
A heat wave warning has been issued throughout the country.

2188
01:19:04,532 --> 01:19:07,461
Here, the Suwon KT Wiz Park is filled with even more heat...

2189
01:19:07,462 --> 01:19:09,371
- as the second game proceeds... - There's no script,

2190
01:19:09,372 --> 01:19:10,431
and he just says whatever...

2191
01:19:10,432 --> 01:19:11,472
- he thinks of. - There's no script at all.

2192
01:19:11,742 --> 01:19:14,901
Have you thought of what to say for the opening?

2193
01:19:14,902 --> 01:19:17,842
Yes, I prepared a simple one.

2194
01:19:19,642 --> 01:19:23,952
(The commentary he's making for the first time at the stadium)

2195
01:19:25,752 --> 01:19:27,722
KT Wiz that's aiming for third place...

2196
01:19:27,952 --> 01:19:31,761
and Samsung Lions aiming for fifth place...

2197
01:19:31,762 --> 01:19:35,491
are fighting against each other in the scorching heat of 35°C.

2198
01:19:35,492 --> 01:19:38,162
Yesterday, Son Dong Hyun appeared in the top of the 9th inning,

2199
01:19:38,402 --> 01:19:40,531
and he showed a magical three-strikeout,

2200
01:19:40,532 --> 01:19:42,271
leading KT Wiz to victory.

2201
01:19:42,272 --> 01:19:43,932
Will Samsung Lions be able...

2202
01:19:44,302 --> 01:19:46,171
to take victory and stop themselves...

2203
01:19:46,172 --> 01:19:48,141
- from three consecutive losses? - He's good.

2204
01:19:48,142 --> 01:19:50,441
Or will KT Wiz continue its winning streak for the fifth time...

2205
01:19:50,442 --> 01:19:52,882
and get a step closer to third place?

2206
01:19:52,982 --> 01:19:54,611
Let us find out together.

2207
01:19:54,612 --> 01:19:56,712
- Gosh, that was neat, indeed. - Was it okay?

2208
01:19:57,912 --> 01:19:59,121
The opening comment was amazing.

2209
01:19:59,122 --> 01:20:00,222
- Really? - Yes.

2210
01:20:00,582 --> 01:20:02,251
(Relieved)

2211
01:20:02,252 --> 01:20:05,222
I made use of 3rd and 5th place with 35°C.

2212
01:20:05,422 --> 01:20:06,422
That was nice.

2213
01:20:07,222 --> 01:20:08,262
That was nice.

2214
01:20:08,762 --> 01:20:10,191
- That was so forced. - Wait.

2215
01:20:10,192 --> 01:20:11,561
- That was related? - That was...

2216
01:20:11,562 --> 01:20:12,731
- I just found out. - I just found out.

2217
01:20:12,732 --> 01:20:14,831
- Wait. You used 3 and 5 like that? - Who would know?

2218
01:20:14,832 --> 01:20:16,401
Baseball fans know.

2219
01:20:16,402 --> 01:20:17,471
- Baseball fans... - You could've also said...

2220
01:20:17,472 --> 01:20:18,541
the fans came in groups of 3 and 5.

2221
01:20:18,542 --> 01:20:20,241
- I could've used that. - Yes, groups of 3 and 5.

2222
01:20:20,242 --> 01:20:21,811
If you keep sticking to such humor,

2223
01:20:21,812 --> 01:20:23,911
fans might look forward to it.

2224
01:20:23,912 --> 01:20:26,381
- "What will he say today?" - Right? That's right.

2225
01:20:26,382 --> 01:20:29,611
One of the sportscasters of the KBO League...

2226
01:20:29,612 --> 01:20:32,221
always reads a poem during the opening.

2227
01:20:32,222 --> 01:20:34,281
He became really famous for it.

2228
01:20:34,282 --> 01:20:36,491
- Just like that, if you have... - Like your own signature.

2229
01:20:36,492 --> 01:20:37,821
- Yes, like a signature comment. - That's right.

2230
01:20:37,822 --> 01:20:39,021
- That'd be nice. - It's like your character.

2231
01:20:39,022 --> 01:20:40,462
You need a character of your own.

2232
01:20:40,662 --> 01:20:42,992
(The game begins with Kang Yong's impressive opening.)

2233
01:20:43,232 --> 01:20:45,201
Great pitches by both teams' starting pitchers...

2234
01:20:45,202 --> 01:20:47,662
and the infielders' defense.

2235
01:20:48,202 --> 01:20:50,102
(Staring)

2236
01:20:50,902 --> 01:20:53,602
(Suddenly getting up)

2237
01:20:55,672 --> 01:20:57,772
- What could it be? - It smells amazing.

2238
01:20:59,442 --> 01:21:00,881
- That looks like chicken. - Chicken?

2239
01:21:00,882 --> 01:21:02,082
(For his senior who used his holiday to study with him)

2240
01:21:02,382 --> 01:21:03,711
- You need to eat well... - It's chicken.

2241
01:21:03,712 --> 01:21:05,251
To talk for like 3 to 4 hours.

2242
01:21:05,252 --> 01:21:06,821
Chickens at baseball stadiums are the best.

2243
01:21:06,822 --> 01:21:07,852
That's true.

2244
01:21:08,222 --> 01:21:10,822
It's my first time having chicken at a commentary booth.

2245
01:21:11,292 --> 01:21:13,362
- Even if we have chicken... - It looks so good.

2246
01:21:13,492 --> 01:21:15,332
You need to focus...

2247
01:21:15,562 --> 01:21:17,131
- on the game. - Yes.

2248
01:21:17,132 --> 01:21:18,531
All right?

2249
01:21:18,532 --> 01:21:20,402
- A fly out to center field. - A fly out to center field.

2250
01:21:23,402 --> 01:21:26,742
(His eyes focus on the game, just as his senior advised.)

2251
01:21:29,212 --> 01:21:31,012
(Shall I take a bite?)

2252
01:21:31,042 --> 01:21:32,042
(Screaming)

2253
01:21:32,043 --> 01:21:33,182
What's going on?

2254
01:21:33,812 --> 01:21:34,812
(Screaming)

2255
01:21:37,182 --> 01:21:39,881
(The ball slipped between the 3rd baseman and the shortstop.)

2256
01:21:39,882 --> 01:21:42,122
- It's a hit. - It slipped in between.

2257
01:21:42,492 --> 01:21:44,522
- Kang Yong, this is important. - Yes.

2258
01:21:44,722 --> 01:21:45,922
What was that?

2259
01:21:46,592 --> 01:21:47,921
What was important?

2260
01:21:47,922 --> 01:21:49,431
A ball that slipped between the third baseman and the shortstop.

2261
01:21:49,432 --> 01:21:51,462
It wasn't just a hit. What do you call it?

2262
01:21:52,702 --> 01:21:53,932
What kind of hit was it?

2263
01:21:54,532 --> 01:21:56,201
- It looks like he was eating, - From the center?

2264
01:21:56,202 --> 01:21:57,802
- but he was watching everything. - Today...

2265
01:21:58,002 --> 01:21:59,801
It was the first hit for both teams.

2266
01:21:59,802 --> 01:22:01,972
You need to point that out.

2267
01:22:02,242 --> 01:22:04,011
- I see. - You should point out what it is.

2268
01:22:04,012 --> 01:22:05,642
(He writes it down on the sheet right away.)

2269
01:22:06,942 --> 01:22:09,282
It was thrown to the second baseman, Yang Do Geun.

2270
01:22:09,482 --> 01:22:12,022
Catching it lightly, it's a two-out.

2271
01:22:12,252 --> 01:22:13,321
The second baseman, Kim Seong Yoon catches it...

2272
01:22:13,322 --> 01:22:14,382
and throws it to the first base.

2273
01:22:14,652 --> 01:22:15,692
That's it.

2274
01:22:16,122 --> 01:22:19,622
That was good, but you said something wrong.

2275
01:22:20,722 --> 01:22:22,061
- What? - That was good, but...

2276
01:22:22,062 --> 01:22:23,062
- You said something wrong? - Just now.

2277
01:22:23,063 --> 01:22:24,132
Who was the second baseman?

2278
01:22:25,462 --> 01:22:27,032
Ryu Ji Hyeok.

2279
01:22:27,162 --> 01:22:28,332
The second baseman was...

2280
01:22:28,672 --> 01:22:30,002
- Yang Do Geun. I see. - Yang Do Geun.

2281
01:22:30,132 --> 01:22:31,671
- When the one on the outfield... - He said the wrong name?

2282
01:22:31,672 --> 01:22:33,471
Comes into the infield...

2283
01:22:33,472 --> 01:22:35,812
(I made a mistake on the name.)

2284
01:22:36,312 --> 01:22:38,941
I get that you didn't have time,

2285
01:22:38,942 --> 01:22:40,912
but you can't make a mistake on their names.

2286
01:22:41,512 --> 01:22:43,611
- You'll be in big trouble. - This is not right.

2287
01:22:43,612 --> 01:22:44,981
You can never make a mistake on this.

2288
01:22:44,982 --> 01:22:46,281
You can't.

2289
01:22:46,282 --> 01:22:48,281
A different player was in the position of the player...

2290
01:22:48,282 --> 01:22:49,451
who played the day before.

2291
01:22:49,452 --> 01:22:50,951
- So I thought he'd be there. - No.

2292
01:22:50,952 --> 01:22:52,521
- So I was... - You can't do that.

2293
01:22:52,522 --> 01:22:54,791
Quite careless when I made that comment.

2294
01:22:54,792 --> 01:22:56,191
The batter with 2 outs and a runner on the 1st and 2nd base.

2295
01:22:56,192 --> 01:22:58,532
On the 2nd base is Yang Do Geun, and on the 1st base...

2296
01:22:58,962 --> 01:23:00,201
(Oh, dear...)

2297
01:23:00,202 --> 01:23:02,601
On the 2nd base is Lee Jae Hyeon, and on the 1st base is Yang Do Geun.

2298
01:23:02,602 --> 01:23:05,001
It's their first crisis and...

2299
01:23:05,002 --> 01:23:06,302
(His thoughts are all jumbled as he's focusing on the names.)

2300
01:23:06,442 --> 01:23:07,571
(Sighing)

2301
01:23:07,572 --> 01:23:09,111
It's his crisis!

2302
01:23:09,112 --> 01:23:11,712
What should I call it? A crisis and a chance at the same time?

2303
01:23:12,912 --> 01:23:14,441
- What's that? - What should I call it?

2304
01:23:14,442 --> 01:23:15,582
Is it a foreign movie dubbing?

2305
01:23:15,752 --> 01:23:17,211
Are you dubbing or something?

2306
01:23:17,212 --> 01:23:19,481
- "My teacher told me." - What should I call it?

2307
01:23:19,482 --> 01:23:21,421
"James told me."

2308
01:23:21,422 --> 01:23:23,291
How can a sportscaster go, "What should I call it?"

2309
01:23:23,292 --> 01:23:25,021
- "What should I call it?" - "What should I call it?"

2310
01:23:25,022 --> 01:23:26,861
It gets you immersed, though.

2311
01:23:26,862 --> 01:23:28,061
- You're right. - You're right.

2312
01:23:28,062 --> 01:23:29,992
It really is like a dubbing for an American movie.

2313
01:23:30,032 --> 01:23:31,592
That's incredible.

2314
01:23:31,892 --> 01:23:34,832
It's a flyball for Jurado.

2315
01:23:35,232 --> 01:23:36,702
Even I'm burning inside.

2316
01:23:37,902 --> 01:23:39,502
- You missed it, right? - Yes, I did.

2317
01:23:40,942 --> 01:23:43,472
(He even makes a mistake recording while focusing on the names.)

2318
01:23:43,842 --> 01:23:46,341
You need to write it down real-time.

2319
01:23:46,342 --> 01:23:47,511
You must be really busy.

2320
01:23:47,512 --> 01:23:49,451
- He steps out after... - Gosh, it's really hard.

2321
01:23:49,452 --> 01:23:51,611
Write it down right away. See if you made any mistakes.

2322
01:23:51,612 --> 01:23:53,322
Remember where all the defenders are.

2323
01:23:53,452 --> 01:23:55,182
You must practice a lot.

2324
01:23:55,652 --> 01:23:57,192
I can't seem to go on.

2325
01:23:58,592 --> 01:24:00,161
It's only natural.

2326
01:24:00,162 --> 01:24:01,362
Seriously.

2327
01:24:01,462 --> 01:24:02,631
I felt lost.

2328
01:24:02,632 --> 01:24:04,391
There were so many things to keep an eye on.

2329
01:24:04,392 --> 01:24:06,061
I had to check the scoreboard too.

2330
01:24:06,062 --> 01:24:07,232
That's right.

2331
01:24:08,002 --> 01:24:09,472
And I had to watch the screens in front of me.

2332
01:24:10,732 --> 01:24:13,271
- I had to look at the sheets too. - Memorizing names is...

2333
01:24:13,272 --> 01:24:14,571
You can't make a mistake on the names.

2334
01:24:14,572 --> 01:24:16,841
And I had to think of what to say too.

2335
01:24:16,842 --> 01:24:18,611
There were so many things to do.

2336
01:24:18,612 --> 01:24:20,711
I didn't know what to sort out first...

2337
01:24:20,712 --> 01:24:22,511
and what to say first.

2338
01:24:22,512 --> 01:24:24,082
I was really lost.

2339
01:24:24,882 --> 01:24:27,682
(He can't even eat the chicken.)

2340
01:24:28,452 --> 01:24:31,421
(His hand is busy, and so are his eyes.)

2341
01:24:31,422 --> 01:24:33,491
You need to keep mentioning their names.

2342
01:24:33,492 --> 01:24:35,321
- Gosh, it's hard. - That must be really hard.

2343
01:24:35,322 --> 01:24:37,591
You need to like baseball...

2344
01:24:37,592 --> 01:24:39,102
to be able to keep up.

2345
01:24:41,132 --> 01:24:42,801
It's a ground ball. The third baseman advances,

2346
01:24:42,802 --> 01:24:45,231
but Hur Kyoung Min catches the difficult ball...

2347
01:24:45,232 --> 01:24:46,872
and throws it to the first base. He's out.

2348
01:24:47,172 --> 01:24:48,472
- That was good. - Here,

2349
01:24:48,912 --> 01:24:50,711
you should raise your energy level up.

2350
01:24:50,712 --> 01:24:52,381
He caught it. It was a difficult ground ball.

2351
01:24:52,382 --> 01:24:54,012
Hur Kyoung Min! My gosh.

2352
01:24:54,112 --> 01:24:56,812
Without having to use descriptive words,

2353
01:24:57,152 --> 01:25:00,122
you need to leave an impact. You don't have to elaborate.

2354
01:25:00,322 --> 01:25:02,851
The difficult ground ball on the third base. Hur Kyoung Min!

2355
01:25:02,852 --> 01:25:04,992
Hur Kyoung Min is great, indeed!

2356
01:25:05,222 --> 01:25:07,121
- That was a perfect defense. - I see.

2357
01:25:07,122 --> 01:25:08,932
- He didn't say much. - Right.

2358
01:25:09,262 --> 01:25:11,062
- You can just keep it simple. - Okay.

2359
01:25:12,102 --> 01:25:14,462
His season batting average is 0.265.

2360
01:25:14,832 --> 01:25:17,402
He's proving himself as the ace of starting players.

2361
01:25:18,432 --> 01:25:21,471
Using the quick feet of a center fielder,

2362
01:25:21,472 --> 01:25:23,642
he treated it well. That's two outs.

2363
01:25:23,742 --> 01:25:26,912
Sportscaster Ko Kang Yong knows what to point out.

2364
01:25:27,712 --> 01:25:28,952
He's moved.

2365
01:25:30,882 --> 01:25:33,382
I feel more relaxed now.

2366
01:25:34,222 --> 01:25:36,122
Swing and miss! Three-strikeout.

2367
01:25:36,452 --> 01:25:39,261
So Hyeong Jun escapes a crisis.

2368
01:25:39,262 --> 01:25:41,162
Gosh, that's nice.

2369
01:25:41,622 --> 01:25:42,791
(Feeling proud of himself)

2370
01:25:42,792 --> 01:25:44,531
- He compliments a lot. - From here,

2371
01:25:44,532 --> 01:25:46,332
you don't need to say much.

2372
01:25:46,462 --> 01:25:47,762
Discuss whether they'll be able to score or not.

2373
01:25:48,062 --> 01:25:50,532
(It's 0 to 0 even in the 7th inning.)

2374
01:25:51,972 --> 01:25:53,901
(Fans from both teams are tense.)

2375
01:25:53,902 --> 01:25:56,172
KT Wiz positions in for defense.

2376
01:25:57,312 --> 01:25:59,011
It's nerve-racking.

2377
01:25:59,012 --> 01:26:00,941
All the runners are in scoring positions.

2378
01:26:00,942 --> 01:26:02,382
One out and runners on third and second.

2379
01:26:03,052 --> 01:26:05,921
KT Wiz isn't willing to give any score,

2380
01:26:05,922 --> 01:26:07,351
based on their defense.

2381
01:26:07,352 --> 01:26:09,621
We can see such determination.

2382
01:26:09,622 --> 01:26:11,392
That they will never concede.

2383
01:26:12,392 --> 01:26:13,862
(And...)

2384
01:26:13,892 --> 01:26:15,361
That's a big hit.

2385
01:26:15,362 --> 01:26:16,591
- He hit it. - They made it.

2386
01:26:16,592 --> 01:26:18,802
(It's their first score of the day.)

2387
01:26:19,102 --> 01:26:21,962
He hit the fifth pitch, and the ball goes to the center.

2388
01:26:22,172 --> 01:26:23,531
The runner on the third base...

2389
01:26:23,532 --> 01:26:26,342
and the runner on the second base score as well.

2390
01:26:26,542 --> 01:26:29,212
The batter is taken out on the second base.

2391
01:26:31,112 --> 01:26:33,342
Samsung Lions scores first.

2392
01:26:33,442 --> 01:26:34,512
(Glancing)

2393
01:26:34,682 --> 01:26:37,182
(Staring at the scoreboard)

2394
01:26:37,482 --> 01:26:39,252
Samsung Lions leads with a score of 2 to 0.

2395
01:26:39,522 --> 01:26:41,082
(Thumbs up)

2396
01:26:41,682 --> 01:26:42,692
Good.

2397
01:26:43,292 --> 01:26:44,292
Well done.

2398
01:26:44,293 --> 01:26:46,461
- Write down the scores as well. - Yes. Right.

2399
01:26:46,462 --> 01:26:48,291
There. You have so many things to do.

2400
01:26:48,292 --> 01:26:49,961
He'll catch up really soon since he has a nice tone.

2401
01:26:49,962 --> 01:26:51,662
His tone is very catchy.

2402
01:26:52,802 --> 01:26:56,302
The Samsung Lions fans are buzzing.

2403
01:26:56,372 --> 01:26:57,731
- No one is sitting... - It's getting heated.

2404
01:26:57,732 --> 01:26:59,041
- except for KT Wiz fans. - The momentum shifted.

2405
01:26:59,042 --> 01:27:00,042
You're right.

2406
01:27:00,043 --> 01:27:01,842
- They finally scored. - Yes.

2407
01:27:02,042 --> 01:27:04,371
So it's better to shout.

2408
01:27:04,372 --> 01:27:05,372
- I see. - Yes.

2409
01:27:05,542 --> 01:27:07,012
You can shout all you want.

2410
01:27:07,482 --> 01:27:08,881
It's going high.

2411
01:27:08,882 --> 01:27:11,181
It's going behind the center fielder.

2412
01:27:11,182 --> 01:27:13,922
It went past the fence.

2413
01:27:14,422 --> 01:27:16,651
Kim Young Woong puts the game out.

2414
01:27:16,652 --> 01:27:17,891
- That's great. - It's...

2415
01:27:17,892 --> 01:27:19,492
- a three-run home run. - How can he say that right away?

2416
01:27:20,262 --> 01:27:22,692
It's 9 to 0. Samsung Lions is leading.

2417
01:27:24,292 --> 01:27:28,402
(Thanks to Na Jin's coaching, he smoothly says his comments.)

2418
01:27:28,602 --> 01:27:29,671
He hit it.

2419
01:27:29,672 --> 01:27:32,132
(They got up from their seats as things got heated.)

2420
01:27:32,472 --> 01:27:35,372
(He comments on top of his lungs while standing.)

2421
01:27:35,502 --> 01:27:38,441
It goes beyond the second baseman.

2422
01:27:38,442 --> 01:27:40,241
(Kang Yong becomes more and more confident.)

2423
01:27:40,242 --> 01:27:43,782
Even the second baseman scores.

2424
01:27:43,882 --> 01:27:47,852
I've watched sports games in person since 2003.

2425
01:27:48,122 --> 01:27:50,852
I watched Jeonju KCC's basketball game in Jeonju Gymnasium.

2426
01:27:51,392 --> 01:27:53,092
I was a little boy then.

2427
01:27:53,592 --> 01:27:56,592
I didn't go to cram school to watch basketball games.

2428
01:27:56,932 --> 01:27:59,532
I couldn't believe it.

2429
01:27:59,832 --> 01:28:02,832
Actually, I have to go to work really early in the morning.

2430
01:28:03,102 --> 01:28:05,801
I studied sports broadcasting until late in the evening,

2431
01:28:05,802 --> 01:28:07,872
and I even went to the stadium.

2432
01:28:08,072 --> 01:28:09,842
Still, it's fine for me.

2433
01:28:10,542 --> 01:28:11,842
Because I'm doing what I like,

2434
01:28:12,112 --> 01:28:13,182
I'm really happy.

2435
01:28:14,312 --> 01:28:15,381
The second hitter hits it.

2436
01:28:15,382 --> 01:28:18,352
(He happily spent his holiday by working.)

2437
01:28:19,652 --> 01:28:23,752
(I'm Happy Because I Do What I Love)

2438
01:28:24,092 --> 01:28:25,692
(Next story)

2439
01:28:29,062 --> 01:28:31,831
(Today, )

2440
01:28:31,832 --> 01:28:33,632
(I'm going back...)

2441
01:28:34,702 --> 01:28:36,031
(to my old self.)

2442
01:28:36,032 --> 01:28:37,932
I got a scuba diving certification.

2443
01:28:38,402 --> 01:28:40,702
(Recalling the old days when he was one with water)

2444
01:28:43,572 --> 01:28:47,512
(He returns to the sea.)

2445
01:28:47,642 --> 01:28:49,251
It's both scary and nerve-racking.

2446
01:28:49,252 --> 01:28:50,452
(He'd freely float around.)

2447
01:28:51,452 --> 01:28:53,681
(Greeting the friends from the same hometown)

2448
01:28:53,682 --> 01:28:54,921
(Abalone)

2449
01:28:54,922 --> 01:28:56,121
I felt like I became a dugong.

2450
01:28:56,122 --> 01:28:58,892
(The Return of Prince Dugong)

2451
01:28:59,892 --> 01:29:01,292
(I believe there are past lives.)

2452
01:29:02,062 --> 01:29:03,362
(Isn't it amazing that you're alive right now?)

2453
01:29:04,162 --> 01:29:06,062
(Why am I alive now, of all times?)

2454
01:29:07,002 --> 01:29:08,032
(What I want to say...)

2455
01:29:09,402 --> 01:29:10,801
(Maybe...)

2456
01:29:10,802 --> 01:29:13,172
(I was a dinosaur.)

2457
01:29:13,272 --> 01:29:14,872
(Maybe dinosaur genes have been passed down.)

2458
01:29:16,312 --> 01:29:18,041
(What's the truth?)

2459
01:29:18,042 --> 01:29:19,212
(Curious)

2460
01:29:19,812 --> 01:29:20,882
(Docent)

2461
01:29:21,142 --> 01:29:23,112
(Teach me more about dinosaurs, Mr. Docent.)

2462
01:29:23,552 --> 01:29:24,752
(Even a giant ammonite)

2463
01:29:24,882 --> 01:29:26,482
(Oh, they eat ammonites.)

2464
01:29:27,352 --> 01:29:28,622
(Step by step)

2465
01:29:29,222 --> 01:29:30,752
(He walks into the world of dinosaurs.)

2466
01:29:31,222 --> 01:29:32,562
(Serious)

2467
01:29:33,062 --> 01:29:35,161
(Where I'm living...)

2468
01:29:35,162 --> 01:29:36,162
Dinosaurs.

2469
01:29:36,162 --> 01:29:37,162
(Summoning dinosaurs)

2470
01:29:37,662 --> 01:29:38,832
(The Jurassic Park opens.)

2471
01:29:39,602 --> 01:29:43,472
(The Birth of Juranosaurus)
